This is no time
for explanations.

717
00:33:43,933 --> 00:33:46,667
- Let me explain--
- man from earth,

718
00:33:46,700 --> 00:33:51,400
you are accused
of causing injury
to one of our people.

719
00:33:51,433 --> 00:33:54,167
I thought I was being attacked,
and I defended myself.

720
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,933
With courage and nudeness.

721
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:58,233
I didn't wanna come
to your world.

722
00:33:58,267 --> 00:34:00,500
I lost control of my ship.

723
00:34:00,533 --> 00:34:03,467
It was like being pulled
toward your planet

724
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:06,000
by an enormous
gravitational force.

725
00:34:06,033 --> 00:34:10,267
- Thank you.
- You were. When you came into
our path of travel.

726
00:34:10,300 --> 00:34:12,033
Path of travel...

727
00:34:12,067 --> 00:34:14,967
Uh, is that the path
you travel on?

728
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:16,667
Phantom planet...

729
00:34:16,700 --> 00:34:20,467
We managed, just in time,
to control your landing

730
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:23,800
by releasing the pressure
in our space warp.

731
00:34:23,833 --> 00:34:25,567
I don't understand.

732
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:28,433
There are many things
you will not understand here.

733
00:34:28,467 --> 00:34:29,933
Big and obvious doorknob.

734
00:34:29,967 --> 00:34:31,967
Maybe in time, you shall.

735
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:33,667
In time?

736
00:34:33,700 --> 00:34:35,233
That is correct.

737
00:34:35,267 --> 00:34:37,233
The jury will now vote

738
00:34:37,267 --> 00:34:39,967
and find you guilty
or not guilty

739
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:44,200
for inflicting injury
on a rheton man.

740
00:34:44,233 --> 00:34:47,467
We find him guilty, guilty!
G-u-i-l-t-y.

741
00:34:47,500 --> 00:34:49,600
Guilty, guilty!
G-u-i-l-t-y.

742
00:34:49,633 --> 00:34:52,367
Whoo! Yay!

743
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:57,033
The guilty party will receive
a dream trip to sunny Cancun.

744
00:34:57,067 --> 00:35:00,367
- Inherit the wow!
- The verdict, judge.

745
00:35:00,400 --> 00:35:03,600
We wrote it out
on our eyebrow pencil shavings.

746
00:35:05,033 --> 00:35:09,467
Uh, I'll take a peppermint one,
I guess.

747
00:35:09,500 --> 00:35:12,867
- I find you guilty as charged.
- Hmm?

748
00:35:12,900 --> 00:35:15,367
You are now a free subject
of rheton.

749
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:18,267
The jury is dismissed.

750
00:35:18,300 --> 00:35:19,733
That is all.

751
00:35:19,767 --> 00:35:21,467
You just simmer down, mister.

752
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:24,300
You are now a free subject
of rheton.

753
00:35:24,333 --> 00:35:25,667
That is not all.

754
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:27,867
Listen, I don't know
what kind of a place this is,

755
00:35:27,900 --> 00:35:29,933
but you must have some kind
of law here.

756
00:35:29,967 --> 00:35:31,800
This planet pulled me to it.

757
00:35:31,833 --> 00:35:33,533
I didn't come here by choice.

758
00:35:33,567 --> 00:35:38,033
By being here, you cannot
be permitted to leave it.

759
00:35:38,067 --> 00:35:41,767
We must keep our security
at any cost,

760
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:45,200
so I must pronounce you guilty.

761
00:35:45,233 --> 00:35:46,533
Yeah, what dad says.

762
00:35:46,567 --> 00:35:50,567
No penalties will be lodged
against you.

763
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:53,500
But you must become
a subject of rheton.

764
00:35:53,533 --> 00:35:55,867
You get a dress like mine.

765
00:35:55,900 --> 00:35:57,600
Trial is concluded.

766
00:35:57,633 --> 00:35:59,567
Nothing is concluded.

767
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,367
What is this?
First I'm found guilty

768
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:03,600
of something
that's not my fault,
and then I'm set free.

769
00:36:03,633 --> 00:36:06,933
Well, free to go where?
Back to my world
six inches tall?

770
00:36:06,967 --> 00:36:09,867
Don't worry.
No harm will come to you.

771
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:12,433
Just don't step
in our many bear traps.

772
00:36:12,467 --> 00:36:15,333
- I'm liara, sessom's daughter.
- Ooh.

773
00:36:15,367 --> 00:36:17,533
- I'll show you
to your quarters.
- [Imitating robotic whirring]

774
00:36:17,567 --> 00:36:19,267
Come.
We'll talk on the way.

775
00:36:23,867 --> 00:36:27,433
And Wednesday Addams
is crestfallen.

776
00:36:27,467 --> 00:36:29,000
What has happened to me?

777
00:36:29,033 --> 00:36:30,933
You mean your size?

778
00:36:30,967 --> 00:36:33,800
Well, our atmosphere,
together with some acceleration

779
00:36:33,833 --> 00:36:36,900
from our gravitational control,
has reduced you to normal.

780
00:36:36,933 --> 00:36:39,000
- Normal?
- Normal for US.

781
00:36:39,033 --> 00:36:42,300
You see, everything here
is in proportion
to our planet's size.

782
00:36:42,333 --> 00:36:44,700
- Really?
- We know several worlds

783
00:36:44,733 --> 00:36:46,967
that have creatures
larger or smaller

784
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,467
according to the size
of their world.

785
00:36:48,500 --> 00:36:50,133
You're explaining it
to a garden slug.

786
00:36:50,167 --> 00:36:51,633
Do you feel any different?

787
00:36:51,667 --> 00:36:53,500
No, but it's not
exactly funny to think

788
00:36:53,533 --> 00:36:55,633
that someone on earth
could carry me about
in their pocket.

789
00:36:55,667 --> 00:36:57,633
Oh, well,
that would never happen.

790
00:36:57,667 --> 00:36:59,600
You see,
oxygen in your atmosphere

791
00:36:59,633 --> 00:37:01,967
would restore you immediately
to your regular size.

792
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:04,000
- So people are just balloons?
- Yes.

793
00:37:04,033 --> 00:37:06,000
But either way,
it wouldn't matter.

794
00:37:06,033 --> 00:37:08,433
You'll never see
your world again.

795
00:37:08,467 --> 00:37:11,567
Ha-ha! Burned you good,
astro boy.

796
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:14,433
Hey, your dark-haired friend
seeing anyone?

797
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:18,100
Man, there's no ham left.

798
00:37:18,133 --> 00:37:19,500
Nothing yet?

799
00:37:19,533 --> 00:37:21,433
No, sir.
No contact for two days.

800
00:37:21,467 --> 00:37:22,800
Lunch is ruined.

801
00:37:22,833 --> 00:37:24,733
I'll wait another 24 hours.

802
00:37:24,767 --> 00:37:29,500
Then, with or without orders,
I'm sending out a search party.

803
00:37:29,533 --> 00:37:32,533
[Mike imitating sessom]
And that's why I'm dressed
as Quentin crisp.

804
00:37:32,567 --> 00:37:34,500
- You wanted to see me?
- No.

805
00:37:34,533 --> 00:37:38,967
Yes. Will you excuse me?

806
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:41,933
There seems to be a problem
with your credit card, sir.

807
00:37:41,967 --> 00:37:44,967
- We must talk
about your future.
- Plastics, Benjamin.

808
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,667
Your future on rheton.

809
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:48,667
My future on rheton?

810
00:37:48,700 --> 00:37:52,633
I wanna talk about
getting back to my world.
Back to earth.

811
00:37:52,667 --> 00:37:55,633
I'm afraid that is impossible.

812
00:37:55,667 --> 00:37:57,967
You might as well accept
your fate.

813
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:00,200
Your fate of being
one of US.

814
00:38:00,233 --> 00:38:01,967
And being one of US,

815
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:04,933
you must be productive
in one way or another.

816
00:38:04,967 --> 00:38:06,700
Well, what is it
you want me to do?

817
00:38:06,733 --> 00:38:10,333
You must help US to keep
spaceships from your world
from landing here.

818
00:38:10,367 --> 00:38:13,000
But that's my only hope
of getting back.

819
00:38:13,033 --> 00:38:15,267
- Don't go there, man.
- Forget about it.

820
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:18,400
Sessom rules US,
and we are content.

821
00:38:18,433 --> 00:38:20,167
We're filled with joy! Okay?

822
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:22,833
Now, can't we get on
with this, sessom?

823
00:38:22,867 --> 00:38:24,833
Herron is hasty.

824
00:38:24,867 --> 00:38:26,600
We all are.

825
00:38:26,633 --> 00:38:30,200
Our lives have been changed
so much.

826
00:38:30,233 --> 00:38:33,000
- I would like you
to become acquainted with--
- herbalife.

827
00:38:33,033 --> 00:38:34,167
...our ways.

828
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:35,767
Later, you may choose a wife.

829
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,267
Wives are men here, by the way.

830
00:38:37,300 --> 00:38:39,767
- [Sessom] Liara or zetha.
- Mm.

831
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:43,567
Zetha cannot speak,
but she is a fine woman.

832
00:38:43,600 --> 00:38:47,233
Well, between the two,
it would be difficult
to make a choice.

833
00:38:47,267 --> 00:38:48,567
- Choose her!
- Choose her!

834
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:51,167
- [Sessom] It is no problem.
- Try both.

835
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:52,933
You may take your time.

836
00:38:52,967 --> 00:38:55,267
But once you've made
your choice, remember--

837
00:38:55,300 --> 00:38:56,767
if you touch them,
they explode.

838
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:59,667
...it must not
be taken lightly.

839
00:38:59,700 --> 00:39:02,167
You must be hungry.
Come with me.

840
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:04,133
Liara...

841
00:39:04,167 --> 00:39:07,833
Go now and learn our ways,

842
00:39:07,867 --> 00:39:10,833
and perhaps you may help US
with our problems.

843
00:39:10,867 --> 00:39:13,000
You can decide about this later.

844
00:39:13,033 --> 00:39:14,633
Now you need to eat and rest.

845
00:39:14,667 --> 00:39:17,100
But I wanna stay
and listen to the old guy.

846
00:39:17,133 --> 00:39:18,667
[Chuckles]

847
00:39:18,700 --> 00:39:21,200
Ooh, that's her personal record
for getting nude.

848
00:39:21,233 --> 00:39:22,700
That's amazing! Whoo!

849
00:39:22,733 --> 00:39:24,467
Let her go.

850
00:39:33,367 --> 00:39:35,733
[No audible dialogue]

851
00:39:38,900 --> 00:39:41,500
Yeah, it's all finished.
Now it's just time
for the decals.

852
00:39:41,533 --> 00:39:43,733
- So cool, man!
- Yeah, it is, isn't it?

853
00:39:43,767 --> 00:39:45,733
Wow. What do you--
oh, Pearl's calling.

854
00:39:45,767 --> 00:39:49,367
Aah! Uh, Mike!
Pearl's calling!

855
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:51,733
- Where the heck is he anyway?
- I don't know. I--

856
00:39:51,767 --> 00:39:54,933
oh, wait a minute.
I was supposed to help him
with something, wasn't I?

857
00:39:54,967 --> 00:39:56,600
- I don't know.
- I can't remember.

858
00:39:56,633 --> 00:39:58,667
- Well, I'm sure
he'll cover for me.
- He usually does.

859
00:39:58,700 --> 00:40:01,233
- Anyway, I'm gonna put on
some flames maybe.
- Cool!

860
00:40:01,267 --> 00:40:03,300
- I was thinking
of putting on a skull.
- Oh, yeah!

861
00:40:03,333 --> 00:40:05,133
- "Double-f into triple zed"--
- that's the one that goes...

862
00:40:05,167 --> 00:40:07,600
I simply don't understand that.
This is like--

863
00:40:07,633 --> 00:40:09,267
- hello, toys.
- Oh.

864
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:11,033
As you can see,

865
00:40:11,067 --> 00:40:13,800
our doomsday device
is coming along quite nicely,

866
00:40:13,833 --> 00:40:16,467
and soon the world
will kneel before me...

867
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:19,767
[Ghostly voice wailing,
chain rattling]

868
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:21,700
- What was that?
- I-I don't know.

869
00:40:21,733 --> 00:40:24,067
- It sounds like...
- [Ghostly voice,
chain rattling continues]

870
00:40:24,100 --> 00:40:26,900
It sounds like some horrible
disembodied spirit.

871
00:40:26,933 --> 00:40:28,433
[Ghostly voice,
chain rattling intensifies]

872
00:40:28,467 --> 00:40:30,567
It's getting closer.

873
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:32,833
This haunted tomb of a castle
has produced

874
00:40:32,867 --> 00:40:35,567
some ancient,
hellish hell spawn

875
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:39,167
to-- to wreak vengeance on US
for our wicked ways.

876
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:40,667
I'm not ready to die.

877
00:40:40,700 --> 00:40:43,733
I just wanna rule the world.
Is that wrong?

878
00:40:43,767 --> 00:40:45,267
Oh, it is among US.

879
00:40:45,300 --> 00:40:47,333
- Oh, Pearl, hold me.
- Aah!

880
00:40:47,367 --> 00:40:50,300
Embrace me
in this moment of oblivion.

881
00:40:50,333 --> 00:40:52,700
- Oh-ho-ho, we're doomed.
- [Muttering]

882
00:40:52,733 --> 00:40:55,667
Oh, man, am I tired.
[Laughs]

883
00:40:55,700 --> 00:40:59,033
I feel like I'm dragging a safe.
I need a nap.

884
00:40:59,067 --> 00:41:01,433
What the hell is this?

885
00:41:01,467 --> 00:41:02,567
[Laughs]

886
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:04,067
Ain't that the berries!

887
00:41:04,100 --> 00:41:06,800
I've been dragging this chain
all over the dang castle.

888
00:41:06,833 --> 00:41:09,000
Whoo! No wonder I'm so tired.

889
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:11,600
[Laughing]

890
00:41:11,633 --> 00:41:12,767
Ohh!

891
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:15,733
Oh!
[Mutters]

892
00:41:15,767 --> 00:41:19,067
- Brain guy.
- Madam.

893
00:41:19,100 --> 00:41:23,133
Get the pipe wrench,
and then murder bobo, won't you?

894
00:41:23,167 --> 00:41:26,067
[Bobo snoring]

895
00:41:26,100 --> 00:41:27,767
Glad to.

896
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:29,933
Thank you.

897
00:41:29,967 --> 00:41:31,933
What are you looking at?

898
00:41:31,967 --> 00:41:34,000
Get back into that theater, you!

899
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:36,700
Yeah. Then I'm gonna throw on
some baby moon hubcaps.

900
00:41:36,733 --> 00:41:38,733
- Oh, man, that'll be so--
- it's gonna look so cool.

901
00:41:38,767 --> 00:41:41,100
- What, what, what?
- There's Mike! He's out there!

902
00:41:41,133 --> 00:41:43,967
Doh! Oh, yeah. That's right.
I was supposed to keep
an eye on him.

903
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:45,533
- [Laughing]
- [Laughs] You!

904
00:41:45,567 --> 00:41:47,867
- [Alarm blaring]
- Oh, hey, Mike,
better get your can in here!

905
00:41:47,900 --> 00:41:51,000
- It's movie time!
- Yeah, stop messing around,
Mike! Come on!

906
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:06,267
He's eating the wall.

907
00:42:06,300 --> 00:42:08,567
This is good.
What is it?

908
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:11,600
I think it's the equivalent
of your breadfruit.

909
00:42:11,633 --> 00:42:15,267
We made it chemically for you
since nothing grows here
on this planet.

910
00:42:15,300 --> 00:42:16,900
- Hi, Mike.
- Oh, man.

911
00:42:16,933 --> 00:42:19,067
- Here. Drink this.
It's good for you.
- [Mike muttering]

912
00:42:19,100 --> 00:42:21,100
- It'll help make you rest.
- Thanks, you guys.

913
00:42:21,133 --> 00:42:23,100
- You need it.
- You say nothing grows here.

914
00:42:23,133 --> 00:42:25,733
- Okay.
- Then how do you exist?

915
00:42:25,767 --> 00:42:27,733
Well, our bodies
are so constructed

916
00:42:27,767 --> 00:42:31,133
that we need very little food
because of the air we breathe.

917
00:42:31,167 --> 00:42:33,800
Next scene. Go!

918
00:42:33,833 --> 00:42:36,767
- Feeling better now?
- Well, my neck's a little sore.

919
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:40,900
- I hope so.
- Yes. But I'd like
to get out of here.

920
00:42:40,933 --> 00:42:43,233
Could you untie my legs?

921
00:42:43,267 --> 00:42:46,167
You're a strange one,
frankchapman.

922
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:48,467
- I'm a strange one?
- You're a girl.

923
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:51,200
What about everybody else?

924
00:42:51,233 --> 00:42:53,133
And don't call me frankchapman.

925
00:42:53,167 --> 00:42:56,167
My name is frank Chapman.
Two words.

926
00:42:56,200 --> 00:42:57,867
First word sounds like, um...

927
00:42:57,900 --> 00:43:01,433
Yes. Frank Chapman.

928
00:43:01,467 --> 00:43:04,233
Oh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to be so rough.

929
00:43:04,267 --> 00:43:06,167
It's just that
this is so new to me.

930
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:07,767
Ladies and words and stuff.

931
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:10,167
You know what I'd like to do
if I had a choice?

932
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:12,567
- What?
- I'd like to return
to my ship.

933
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:14,233
Yeah, well,
return to my butt.

934
00:43:14,267 --> 00:43:16,233
Well, that's impossible.

935
00:43:16,267 --> 00:43:19,400
- Then, you see,
I'm still a prisoner.
- Not at all.

936
00:43:19,433 --> 00:43:21,167
You're free to go
anywhere here on rheton.

937
00:43:21,200 --> 00:43:23,800
- All 50 feet.
- Except to my ship.

938
00:43:23,833 --> 00:43:26,967
Your rocket is no longer
on this planet.

939
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:28,467
It was towed.

940
00:43:28,500 --> 00:43:31,267
It was sent off last night
while you were sleeping.

941
00:43:31,300 --> 00:43:33,400
Words are just
bouncing off his skull.
[Chuckles]

942
00:43:35,833 --> 00:43:37,133
[Chatter over radio]

943
00:43:37,167 --> 00:43:39,267
The rescue ship
is in the countdown phase, sir.

944
00:43:39,300 --> 00:43:41,233
They're waiting for
your final operation orders.

945
00:43:41,267 --> 00:43:43,233
Is he listening
to the ball game?

946
00:43:43,267 --> 00:43:45,633
Put me through to the captain
of the rescue ship on launching.

947
00:43:45,667 --> 00:43:48,433
- Yes, sir.
- God, I love caramel.

948
00:43:48,467 --> 00:43:51,233
- Beecher, this is lansfield.
- So?

949
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:52,567
Yes, colonel.

950
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,067
Beecher,
your final instructions

951
00:43:54,100 --> 00:43:56,133
are being teletyped
on your recorders.

952
00:43:56,167 --> 00:43:58,133
- Yes, sir.
- As you know,

953
00:43:58,167 --> 00:44:01,200
something unusual
must've happened
to Chapman and makonnen.

954
00:44:01,233 --> 00:44:03,500
- The rocket tipped over, sir.
- And I don't mind telling you

955
00:44:03,533 --> 00:44:05,900
that it's
of greatest importance
to space travel

956
00:44:05,933 --> 00:44:07,833
that we find out
exactly what happened

957
00:44:07,867 --> 00:44:09,500
to these two men.

958
00:44:09,533 --> 00:44:12,267
So blast off and good luck.

959
00:44:12,300 --> 00:44:13,733
We'll do our best, colonel.

960
00:44:13,767 --> 00:44:16,667
- Don't tell him that!
- [Chuckles]

961
00:44:16,700 --> 00:44:21,200
Anonymous similar guys, away!

962
00:44:21,233 --> 00:44:25,467
So which part of the universe
you wanna search first?

963
00:44:27,700 --> 00:44:30,767
Wow. This is almost as good
as 2001...

964
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:32,767
Nails driven into your eyes!

965
00:44:32,800 --> 00:44:35,200
- [Chuckles]
- [Scoffs]

966
00:44:35,233 --> 00:44:38,900
You know, other captain,
every year, I become
more and more convinced--

967
00:44:38,933 --> 00:44:41,000
- shut up.
- Sorry.

968
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:46,300
Wow. No one told me
about the black ice
out here in space.

969
00:44:46,333 --> 00:44:48,633
[Imitating rocket whirring]

970
00:44:48,667 --> 00:44:50,100
[Whirring stops]

971
00:44:54,033 --> 00:44:55,633
[Mock gasping]

972
00:44:55,667 --> 00:44:58,067
Oh, sorry about
depressurizing the cabin.

973
00:44:58,100 --> 00:45:00,133
Next time, I'll warn you.

974
00:45:00,167 --> 00:45:02,300
[Chuckles]

975
00:45:02,333 --> 00:45:05,833
I can't believe all NASA flights
are nonsmoking now.

976
00:45:05,867 --> 00:45:07,900
[Scoffs]

977
00:45:11,533 --> 00:45:13,567
Oops. Excuse me.
Those lentils.

978
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:16,633
Space batch!

979
00:45:16,667 --> 00:45:19,000
Open the door!
Open the door!

980
00:45:19,033 --> 00:45:20,967
- [Imitates clank]
- Oh!

981
00:45:24,500 --> 00:45:28,533
Hey, collecting
for the march of dimes
is complicated in space.

982
00:45:28,567 --> 00:45:31,167
- Hey, they have
a nice mud room.
- ** [ambient soundtrack music]

983
00:45:31,200 --> 00:45:35,600
- * some guys in space
- ** [humming along]

984
00:45:35,633 --> 00:45:39,100
* some guys in space

985
00:45:39,133 --> 00:45:41,433
Denise, come on.
The car's running.

986
00:45:41,467 --> 00:45:45,067
[Chapman]
I cannot read my position.
I'm gonna try to land.

987
00:45:45,100 --> 00:45:46,233
Denise, come on!

988
00:45:46,267 --> 00:45:48,067
I don't think I'll make it.

989
00:45:48,100 --> 00:45:51,233
If I do,
I'll continue recording.

990
00:45:51,267 --> 00:45:52,567
[Breathing heavily]

991
00:45:52,600 --> 00:45:54,467
[Sniffs]
Oh, it's like a garbage ship
in here.

992
00:45:54,500 --> 00:45:56,400
This is captain frank Chapman,

993
00:45:56,433 --> 00:45:58,000
the pilot of Pegasus iv.

994
00:45:58,033 --> 00:45:59,233
And crew killer.

995
00:45:59,267 --> 00:46:02,000
My ship is being drawn
toward an asteroid.

996
00:46:02,033 --> 00:46:03,900
Instruments completely
out of operation.

997
00:46:03,933 --> 00:46:06,400
Sorry. I ran here.

998
00:46:06,433 --> 00:46:10,200
Man, arithmetic is just hard.

999
00:46:10,233 --> 00:46:12,067
Um, sum...

1000
00:46:12,100 --> 00:46:14,067
I can't work
under these conditions.

1001
00:46:14,100 --> 00:46:17,167
Gorgeous women waiting
to serve my every whim.

1002
00:46:17,200 --> 00:46:19,733
I must know more about
the directional flight machine.

1003
00:46:19,767 --> 00:46:22,333
- When the time comes.
- Well, the time has come.

1004
00:46:22,367 --> 00:46:26,000
- The walrus said.
- I want to speak to sessom,
and right now.

1005
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:27,767
Stupid leach woman.

1006
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:29,833
- Very well.
- Hey.

1007
00:46:29,867 --> 00:46:32,967
Looks like som
is rapidly approaching non.

1008
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:35,333
Mm-hmm.

1009
00:46:35,367 --> 00:46:38,567
[Imitating sessom]
But I think belted at the waist
gives me a slimmer look.

1010
00:46:38,600 --> 00:46:39,933
- Don't you agree?
- [Clears throat]

1011
00:46:39,967 --> 00:46:40,967
Oh.

1012
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:42,467
Father...

1013
00:46:42,500 --> 00:46:45,233
Frank Chapman wishes
to speak with you.

1014
00:46:45,267 --> 00:46:48,433
- Do you want to talk
about liara?
- Mr. President.

1015
00:46:48,467 --> 00:46:50,867
That isn't what I came here
to discuss.

1016
00:46:50,900 --> 00:46:54,867
My work has reached a stage,
and I need to know more
about your gravity control.

1017
00:46:54,900 --> 00:46:57,600
[Quietly]
Anyway, the blouse is on sale
at talbots today only.

1018
00:46:57,633 --> 00:46:59,533
It's too soon.
Now, how do we know

1019
00:46:59,567 --> 00:47:02,033
he's not a spy
for the solarites?

1020
00:47:02,067 --> 00:47:04,833
You're too distrusting, herron.

1021
00:47:04,867 --> 00:47:06,333
Are you a spy for the solarites?

1022
00:47:06,367 --> 00:47:08,533
All right.
You may see it.

1023
00:47:08,567 --> 00:47:10,767
Although I don't know why
in the hell you'd want to.

1024
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:14,633
Let me just lift my skirt.
There it is. Ta-da!

1025
00:47:16,300 --> 00:47:19,567
Now we shall dive
into the mosh pit.

1026
00:47:23,833 --> 00:47:27,000
This came out
of lyndon Johnson's gallbladder.

1027
00:47:28,067 --> 00:47:30,033
- Incredible.
- Edible.

1028
00:47:30,067 --> 00:47:31,700
But how?

1029
00:47:31,733 --> 00:47:33,600
The high density of our planet

1030
00:47:33,633 --> 00:47:36,267
made it possible for US
to advance gravity

1031
00:47:36,300 --> 00:47:39,333
and, therefore,
antigravity theories.

1032
00:47:39,367 --> 00:47:41,333
It's beyond me.

1033
00:47:41,367 --> 00:47:43,267
Einstein was working
on this problem,

1034
00:47:43,300 --> 00:47:45,467
but he died before
he could complete
his investigation.

1035
00:47:45,500 --> 00:47:46,800
I'm trying to work here.

1036
00:47:46,833 --> 00:47:49,367
What causes rheton's
high density?

1037
00:47:49,400 --> 00:47:52,767
The atoms on this planet
have narrower
electronic orbits--

1038
00:47:52,800 --> 00:47:55,500
- uhhh...
- ...Than the atoms
on most other planets.

1039
00:47:55,533 --> 00:47:57,433
The smaller they become,

1040
00:47:57,467 --> 00:47:59,433
the easier it is
for US to control

1041
00:47:59,467 --> 00:48:03,133
and take advantage of positive
and negative gravity.

1042
00:48:03,167 --> 00:48:05,800
Why is rheton getting smaller?

1043
00:48:05,833 --> 00:48:08,433
This planet is slowly
using up the energy

1044
00:48:08,467 --> 00:48:10,733
that holds
the atomic particles together.

1045
00:48:10,767 --> 00:48:13,600
- Oh.
- You mean you might
disintegrate into nothing?

1046
00:48:13,633 --> 00:48:16,133
- Yes, someday--
- when you're older.

1047
00:48:16,167 --> 00:48:18,067
...but it will not be
in our time.

1048
00:48:18,100 --> 00:48:20,467
- Ah.
- Well, I guess it's
the same as on earth.

1049
00:48:20,500 --> 00:48:22,133
We don't seem to worry
that our sun

1050
00:48:22,167 --> 00:48:23,967
might be cooling off
in many millions of years.

1051
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:26,333
Yeah, but danger for US
is that sudden bursts

1052
00:48:26,367 --> 00:48:28,667
of concentrated heat
directed on rheton--

1053
00:48:28,700 --> 00:48:30,400
oh, sure. You're gonna
get that. Oh, yeah.

1054
00:48:30,433 --> 00:48:33,067
...might suddenly speed up
the process of time.

1055
00:48:33,100 --> 00:48:34,867
You think that's possible?

1056
00:48:34,900 --> 00:48:37,200
We have enemies who want
our knowledge of gravity

1057
00:48:37,233 --> 00:48:39,200
and who know our weakness.

1058
00:48:39,233 --> 00:48:40,833
You're expecting an attack?

1059
00:48:40,867 --> 00:48:43,633
When you have enemies,
you always expect an attack.

1060
00:48:43,667 --> 00:48:46,233
Uh, quiet down. I'm putting
my hands over things here.

1061
00:48:46,267 --> 00:48:47,633
[Chuckles]

1062
00:48:49,433 --> 00:48:51,700
Stud service!

1063
00:48:53,467 --> 00:48:54,767
[High-pitched voice]
Eeee!

1064
00:48:54,800 --> 00:48:56,533
Sorry.

1065
00:48:56,567 --> 00:48:59,133
He's just out
for his morning swagger.

1066
00:48:59,167 --> 00:49:00,467
** [humming]

1067
00:49:00,500 --> 00:49:02,800
Huh? Oh, yeah.
Take it off.

1068
00:49:02,833 --> 00:49:05,067
Oh. Sorry, sir.
[Chuckles]

1069
00:49:05,100 --> 00:49:08,367
Sleeping on a big slab
of tuna steak here.

1070
00:49:08,400 --> 00:49:10,167
Hello.

1071
00:49:10,200 --> 00:49:12,733
We're closed.

1072
00:49:12,767 --> 00:49:15,800
How do you sign
"beat it, loser"?

1073
00:49:18,433 --> 00:49:21,333
I'm sorry my waist
is so big for you.

1074
00:49:21,367 --> 00:49:24,567
You wanna play?
I got a banana-seat bike.

1075
00:49:24,600 --> 00:49:26,067
I'm gonna take a walk.

1076
00:49:26,100 --> 00:49:27,633
Stir-fry some vegetables.

1077
00:49:27,667 --> 00:49:29,133
Will you join me?

1078
00:49:29,167 --> 00:49:30,467
We could lick some walls.

1079
00:49:30,500 --> 00:49:31,967
Come on.

1080
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:33,733
Well, I was kind of
doing some stuff.

1081
00:49:33,767 --> 00:49:35,267
I got a lot--
well, okay.

1082
00:49:35,300 --> 00:49:38,200
I'll take a walk with you.

1083
00:49:38,233 --> 00:49:41,533
You know, this is the first time
I've had a chance
to talk to you alone.

1084
00:49:41,567 --> 00:49:43,367
It's almost like you've been
avoiding me or something.

1085
00:49:43,400 --> 00:49:45,833
Let's just walk over here
to the other end of the planet.

1086
00:49:47,000 --> 00:49:48,933
So, do you like anything?

1087
00:49:48,967 --> 00:49:51,700
Or do you know things or...

1088
00:49:51,733 --> 00:49:55,367
Hey, his helmet is now
a major make-out spot
on the planet.

1089
00:49:57,200 --> 00:49:59,100
How is it you're more different
than the others?

1090
00:49:59,133 --> 00:50:00,767
Or less the same,
is what I'm saying.

1091
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:02,767
I don't mean your silence.
I--

1092
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:06,100
I mean, you're warmer,
more sensitive.

1093
00:50:06,133 --> 00:50:08,100
I like potatoes!

1094
00:50:08,133 --> 00:50:11,267
That wasn't really a question,
'cause I know you can't answer.

1095
00:50:11,300 --> 00:50:13,200
So I'll keep talking
and talking.

1096
00:50:13,233 --> 00:50:16,100
I just wanted you to know
how I feel.

1097
00:50:16,133 --> 00:50:17,600
Strange world...

1098
00:50:17,633 --> 00:50:19,100
Anyway, let's get busy!

1099
00:50:19,133 --> 00:50:21,367
I don't wanna hurt, liara.

1100
00:50:21,400 --> 00:50:23,867
- You don't either.
- Yes, I don't.

1101
00:50:23,900 --> 00:50:25,400
No, I do. What?

1102
00:50:25,433 --> 00:50:27,300
I like you.

1103
00:50:27,333 --> 00:50:29,167
And you can't say
you don't like me.

1104
00:50:29,200 --> 00:50:30,733
[Chuckles]

1105
00:50:30,767 --> 00:50:33,367
Let's go check out my armpits.

1106
00:50:35,367 --> 00:50:36,667
Heh-heh-heh.

1107
00:50:36,700 --> 00:50:40,167
I just smeared atomic bomb
in his underpants.

1108
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:44,900
Look at this guy.
George Shultz
is more expressive.

1109
00:50:46,967 --> 00:50:49,433
I have charges to make
against the earthman Chapman.

1110
00:50:49,467 --> 00:50:51,133
Old guy's stoned
on beta-blockers.

1111
00:50:51,167 --> 00:50:53,733
He is imposing himself
both on liara, your daughter,

1112
00:50:53,767 --> 00:50:55,633
and the mute girl, zetha.

1113
00:50:55,667 --> 00:50:57,567
Now, this is an insult
to liara--

1114
00:50:57,600 --> 00:50:59,233
you know I love her--

1115
00:50:59,267 --> 00:51:01,567
and a direct insult to me.

1116
00:51:01,600 --> 00:51:04,300
- I am asking-- rather--
- blandly.

1117
00:51:04,333 --> 00:51:08,100
...i am demanding
your permission
to challenge him to the duel.

1118
00:51:08,133 --> 00:51:10,400
Hey, Betty and Veronica.

1119
00:51:13,700 --> 00:51:16,967
These two are bothering me
with their lady things.

1120
00:51:19,200 --> 00:51:21,167
You sent for me?

1121
00:51:21,200 --> 00:51:26,033
Yes. I have reports about you
that are not good--

1122
00:51:26,067 --> 00:51:27,667
that you're causing
much trouble.

1123
00:51:27,700 --> 00:51:30,267
What am I supposed
to have done now?

1124
00:51:30,300 --> 00:51:32,600
You are forcing your attentions
on liara,

1125
00:51:32,633 --> 00:51:34,267
and then on the mute girl,
zetha.

1126
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:36,300
That's not true.
Why don't you ask them?

1127
00:51:36,333 --> 00:51:37,933
- He lies!
- Silence.

1128
00:51:37,967 --> 00:51:40,000
- I'm the one
in the velvet dress.
- Is it true?

1129
00:51:40,033 --> 00:51:44,033
Has he forced himself
or his attentions upon you?

1130
00:51:44,067 --> 00:51:46,333
[Mike]
That means "yes, oh, yes,
please help me."

1131
00:51:46,367 --> 00:51:47,800
Why would she admit it?

1132
00:51:47,833 --> 00:51:49,867
Perhaps she's afraid of him.

1133
00:51:49,900 --> 00:51:52,300
Being mute,
she's unable to defend herself.

1134
00:51:52,333 --> 00:51:54,300
[Voice similar to Henry Fonda's]
Maybe she's protecting me.

1135
00:51:54,333 --> 00:51:55,700
Henry Fonda.

1136
00:51:55,733 --> 00:51:57,933
Listen, I'm not gonna
be put on trial or questioned

1137
00:51:57,967 --> 00:52:00,900
by you or anyone else
for something I haven't done.

1138
00:52:00,933 --> 00:52:03,133
You know, buddy,
I don't like you.

1139
00:52:03,167 --> 00:52:05,467
Maybe it's a carryover
from earth and not good taste,

1140
00:52:05,500 --> 00:52:07,133
but I'd like to hang one on you.

1141
00:52:07,167 --> 00:52:09,700
- Chapman--
- would you hang one on me?

1142
00:52:09,733 --> 00:52:13,400
...herron has challenged you
to the duel of rheton.

1143
00:52:13,433 --> 00:52:15,800
Do you accept his challenge?

1144
00:52:15,833 --> 00:52:19,233
A duel for what?
What kind of a duel?

1145
00:52:19,267 --> 00:52:21,567
This guy doesn't look
very honest to me.

1146
00:52:21,600 --> 00:52:24,200
A duel of bravery.

1147
00:52:24,233 --> 00:52:26,367
Yeah. Fine, liara.
Anyway--

1148
00:52:26,400 --> 00:52:28,300
you know, Mr. Sessom,

1149
00:52:28,333 --> 00:52:30,567
maybe this duel business
is a good idea.

1150
00:52:30,600 --> 00:52:32,967
- Might clear the air a little.
- Lacquer hair.

1151
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:35,267
So how do we go about it?

1152
00:52:35,300 --> 00:52:38,133
Later, they went about it.

1153
00:52:38,167 --> 00:52:41,067
Uh, you didn't need
to take your shirts off.

1154
00:52:41,100 --> 00:52:43,233
- Herron--
- you're a blue waterfowl.

1155
00:52:43,267 --> 00:52:46,167
...you know the rules
for the duel of rheton.

1156
00:52:46,200 --> 00:52:48,367
But for him,
I'll have to explain

1157
00:52:48,400 --> 00:52:50,367
and show the results.

1158
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:51,933
Chapman, come here.

1159
00:52:51,967 --> 00:52:55,800
He's showing off
his ray bolger physique.

1160
00:52:55,833 --> 00:52:58,733
Those are gravity plates
that we've had placed here.

1161
00:52:58,767 --> 00:53:00,733
Their intensity is so high

1162
00:53:00,767 --> 00:53:03,167
that any object
or any person

1163
00:53:03,200 --> 00:53:05,567
placed on any one of them

1164
00:53:05,600 --> 00:53:07,600
would immediately disintegrate.

1165
00:53:07,633 --> 00:53:09,100
Kind of a dumb purchase, really.

1166
00:53:09,133 --> 00:53:12,033
- Here. Let me show you.
- Let me just dry
my hands first.

1167
00:53:12,067 --> 00:53:14,033
[Whirring]

1168
00:53:15,467 --> 00:53:17,867
This is a meat loaf
we just made.

1169
00:53:17,900 --> 00:53:19,033
[Whirring continues]

1170
00:53:19,067 --> 00:53:22,067
The audience is hemorrhaging.

1171
00:53:22,100 --> 00:53:24,300
[Mock gasping]

1172
00:53:24,333 --> 00:53:27,933
The linoleum tile of doom!

1173
00:53:27,967 --> 00:53:29,867
[Scoffs]
So? My dad has one of those.

1174
00:53:29,900 --> 00:53:33,400
The duel of rheton
is one of physical strength

1175
00:53:33,433 --> 00:53:35,300
and skill.

1176
00:53:35,333 --> 00:53:38,167
- You will use this rod--
- the rod, please.

1177
00:53:38,200 --> 00:53:40,667
...and attempt
to push your opponent

1178
00:53:40,700 --> 00:53:43,467
on top of one of
the gravity plates.

1179
00:53:43,500 --> 00:53:45,467
You saw what happened
to the rock.

1180
00:53:45,500 --> 00:53:47,733
[Imitating Sean Connery]
I starred in it
with Nicholas cage.

1181
00:53:47,767 --> 00:53:50,400
Suck it in, tiny.

1182
00:53:50,433 --> 00:53:51,900
Get ready.

1183
00:53:51,933 --> 00:53:55,867
What I'm saying is,
let's get ready to rumble!

1184
00:53:57,667 --> 00:53:59,633
Put the combat rod
in position.

1185
00:53:59,667 --> 00:54:02,300
Geez! The old guy
calls it his "combat rod"?

1186
00:54:02,333 --> 00:54:04,300
- I can't believe it.
It's disgusting.
- No.

1187
00:54:04,333 --> 00:54:05,800
- [Mike muttering]
- Oh, wait.

1188
00:54:05,833 --> 00:54:08,367
- Is that what
he's talking about?
- Maybe not.

1189
00:54:11,367 --> 00:54:13,800
You also have to fight
around our bike rack.

1190
00:54:13,833 --> 00:54:16,267
They stole that
from al Pacino's football field.

1191
00:54:16,300 --> 00:54:17,400
[Chuckles]

1192
00:54:19,533 --> 00:54:23,333
Uh, we're just gonna
pour some concrete
while you're fighting.

1193
00:54:23,367 --> 00:54:26,833
Wanna just
Indian wrestle instead?

1194
00:54:26,867 --> 00:54:29,333
You know in a few minutes,
they'll be the best of friends,

1195
00:54:29,367 --> 00:54:32,467
slugging back tranya.

1196
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:34,867
They really gotta cooperate
to kill each other.

1197
00:54:34,900 --> 00:54:36,233
[Chuckles]

1198
00:54:36,267 --> 00:54:37,567
Time! Good match.

1199
00:54:37,600 --> 00:54:39,833
At my signal,
you will start the duel.

1200
00:54:41,800 --> 00:54:44,400
There can be no quarter called
and no quarter given.

1201
00:54:44,433 --> 00:54:45,800
We need them for the laundry.

1202
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:47,600
- The fate of the victim--
- [whispers] Sorry.

1203
00:54:47,633 --> 00:54:49,600
...is in the hands
of the Victor.

1204
00:54:49,633 --> 00:54:52,100
The moment has come.

1205
00:54:52,133 --> 00:54:55,933
At my light signal,
you will proceed.

1206
00:54:55,967 --> 00:54:57,467
- [Beeping]
- Uh, was that the signal?

1207
00:54:57,500 --> 00:54:59,333
It was kind of dim.

1208
00:55:00,867 --> 00:55:02,333
- Push.
- Push.

1209
00:55:02,367 --> 00:55:03,333
Hey, boys.

1210
00:55:03,367 --> 00:55:04,833
[All]
Puuush!

1211
00:55:04,867 --> 00:55:06,933
- Push.
- Push.

1212
00:55:06,967 --> 00:55:11,300
Yeah, this'll be on t.V.
If they ever have ESPN 6.

1213
00:55:11,333 --> 00:55:14,333
You can still see combat rod
fights in Mexico City.

1214
00:55:14,367 --> 00:55:16,533
Huh?

1215
00:55:19,033 --> 00:55:21,433
And now, flood the arena.
Did we tell you about that?

1216
00:55:23,600 --> 00:55:25,800
You know, combat rod
used to be great.

1217
00:55:25,833 --> 00:55:27,400
Now there's just
too much money in it.

1218
00:55:27,433 --> 00:55:28,933
- Yeah, it's just
a business now.
- Yeah.

1219
00:55:28,967 --> 00:55:30,567
Too bad.

1220
00:55:31,900 --> 00:55:33,200
[Men grunting]

1221
00:55:33,233 --> 00:55:34,533
** [humming "charge" fanfare]

1222
00:55:34,567 --> 00:55:36,067
Push him on the gravity plate!

1223
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:37,400
** [humming "charge" fanfare]

1224
00:55:37,433 --> 00:55:40,100
Push him on the gravity plate!

1225
00:55:40,133 --> 00:55:41,933
- [Women shouting] Kill him!
- Early cheeseheads.

1226
00:55:41,967 --> 00:55:45,367
[Shouting continues]

1227
00:55:45,400 --> 00:55:48,033
I'm shirtless,
and it's driving them mad.

1228
00:55:48,067 --> 00:55:50,333
Ice the pig.

1229
00:55:55,967 --> 00:55:58,167
- There, there.
- [Chuckles]

1230
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:02,633
- I don't wanna kill you.
- So can you do it?

1231
00:56:02,667 --> 00:56:05,767
- I never did.
- Except that time you ate
the last synthesized breadfruit.

1232
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:08,533
That really cheesed me off.

1233
00:56:08,567 --> 00:56:11,033
The totals on the board
are correct-rect-rect.

1234
00:56:11,067 --> 00:56:13,033
Thank you for attending
plate and skirt day

1235
00:56:13,067 --> 00:56:15,600
here at combat rod park,
park, park.

1236
00:56:17,033 --> 00:56:19,633
You're gonna put
your shirt back on. Yay!

1237
00:56:19,667 --> 00:56:22,033
Hey, girls, you wanna make
a me sandwich?

1238
00:56:22,067 --> 00:56:23,500
Huh?

1239
00:56:25,767 --> 00:56:27,100
Wow.
[Mutters]

1240
00:56:27,133 --> 00:56:28,700
Add that to the Kama Sutra.

1241
00:56:28,733 --> 00:56:31,567
Neither one of them
are touching the ground.
Holy cow.

1242
00:56:31,600 --> 00:56:34,367
Well, let me show you
the China pattern
I registered for.

1243
00:56:34,400 --> 00:56:36,767
And you're gonna love
the kitchen border I picked out.

1244
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:38,767
Why didn't you kill him?

1245
00:56:38,800 --> 00:56:41,767
I didn't want to.
I don't believe in it.

1246
00:56:41,800 --> 00:56:44,100
In this case, killing him
would've accomplished nothing.

1247
00:56:44,133 --> 00:56:46,300
But herron wouldn't have
shown you mercy.

1248
00:56:46,333 --> 00:56:49,667
He'd have killed you
because he wants me.

1249
00:56:49,700 --> 00:56:52,867
But I don't love him.
I love you.

1250
00:56:52,900 --> 00:56:55,433
If you'd felt anything
for either one of US,

1251
00:56:55,467 --> 00:56:57,567
you could've stopped this duel.

1252
00:56:57,600 --> 00:56:59,567
- What?
- You know what I think?

1253
00:56:59,600 --> 00:57:02,000
I think you were waiting to see
which one of US won,

1254
00:57:02,033 --> 00:57:04,000
and then take the one
that was left over.

1255
00:57:04,033 --> 00:57:05,867
No, liara, I don't love you.

1256
00:57:05,900 --> 00:57:07,567
I don't even know
if I like you.

1257
00:57:07,600 --> 00:57:08,967
You get me going
and all, but--

1258
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:10,833
let me tell you this.

1259
00:57:10,867 --> 00:57:13,733
You can't make someone love you.

1260
00:57:13,767 --> 00:57:15,433
It's got to come naturally.

1261
00:57:15,467 --> 00:57:17,333
You can't force it,
you can't command it.

1262
00:57:17,367 --> 00:57:18,833
That's what the judge told me.

1263
00:57:18,867 --> 00:57:20,433
If you do that,
you'll never find it.

1264
00:57:20,467 --> 00:57:22,233
Chicken droppings for the soul.

1265
00:57:22,267 --> 00:57:25,067
This whole thing
is like a nightmare to me.

1266
00:57:25,100 --> 00:57:29,367
I miss my people.
I've got to make some attempt
to get back.

1267
00:57:29,400 --> 00:57:32,033
And if you feel anything for me,
you'll try to help me.

1268
00:57:32,067 --> 00:57:34,367
I feel indifference
tinged with disgust.

1269
00:57:34,400 --> 00:57:35,700
Well, perhaps you're right.

1270
00:57:35,733 --> 00:57:38,700
You are correct, strange-faced
lilliputian astro boy.

1271
00:57:38,733 --> 00:57:40,733
[Chuckles]

1272
00:57:40,767 --> 00:57:42,800
Maybe I can help you.

1273
00:57:42,833 --> 00:57:44,800
Trust me completely.

1274
00:57:44,833 --> 00:57:47,500
[Mock sinister laughter]

1275
00:57:48,600 --> 00:57:51,267
[Laughter continues]

1276
00:57:51,300 --> 00:57:52,767
Okay, now.

1277
00:57:52,800 --> 00:57:54,700
Well, that went really well.

1278
00:57:54,733 --> 00:57:56,467
I think.

1279
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:59,667
Smell this. Does it smell
kind of fishy to you?

1280
00:58:02,133 --> 00:58:04,367
Hey, did you use this
to shave your legs?

1281
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:07,033
[Chuckles]

1282
00:58:07,067 --> 00:58:09,300
As you said,
I don't wanna kill you.

1283
00:58:09,333 --> 00:58:12,833
Just thought I'd wake you up
and tell you that. 'Night.

1284
00:58:12,867 --> 00:58:15,833
You know,
I think I could understand
your somewhat quaint language

1285
00:58:15,867 --> 00:58:17,767
if I were on your earth
a little.

1286
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:20,000
- Why don't you kill me?
- I'm a loser, baby.

1287
00:58:20,033 --> 00:58:22,267
You didn't kill me,
and you had the chance.

1288
00:58:22,300 --> 00:58:23,933
What about the knife?

1289
00:58:23,967 --> 00:58:27,333
This isn't exactly
what I'd call a friendly visit.

1290
00:58:27,367 --> 00:58:28,667
Ow, ow, ow.

1291
00:58:28,700 --> 00:58:30,667
Is this a scene
between two cement blocks?

1292
00:58:30,700 --> 00:58:32,167
Oh, no. They're human,
aren't they?

1293
00:58:32,200 --> 00:58:34,067
If you help me,

1294
00:58:34,100 --> 00:58:37,000
I have a plan where I might
help you to leave our planet.

1295
00:58:37,033 --> 00:58:38,567
Perhaps it will work.

1296
00:58:38,600 --> 00:58:41,633
I don't see
how this is possible.
What about my size?

1297
00:58:41,667 --> 00:58:44,167
You can be
a bowling trophy model.

1298
00:58:44,200 --> 00:58:46,700
I inspected your giant suit,

1299
00:58:46,733 --> 00:58:49,333
and the oxygen tank holds air
from your own world.

1300
00:58:49,367 --> 00:58:51,167
- Isn't that right?
- Yes, of course. But--

1301
00:58:51,200 --> 00:58:53,100
no. Never mind that.
That's not important.

1302
00:58:53,133 --> 00:58:54,967
Don't trouble your odd-shaped
little head about it.

1303
00:58:55,000 --> 00:58:57,767
You see, the whole plan
is based on a theory

1304
00:58:57,800 --> 00:59:00,433
that your people
are searching for you.

1305
00:59:00,467 --> 00:59:03,433
Now, I must get you back
before they attempt
to find you here.

1306
00:59:03,467 --> 00:59:06,433
I know they've been searching
and will eventually
zero in on this planet.

1307
00:59:06,467 --> 00:59:08,633
Just keep telling
yourself that, you dope.

1308
00:59:08,667 --> 00:59:10,933
I think I can
get you back in time.

1309
00:59:10,967 --> 00:59:14,633
- Yes, but, uh--
- look, do you wanna
hop in with me here?

1310
00:59:14,667 --> 00:59:18,333
You're doing this
because of liara, aren't you?

1311
00:59:18,367 --> 00:59:20,533
Yes, I am.
I'm in love with her.

1312
00:59:20,567 --> 00:59:23,333
I show it by stalking her daily.

1313
00:59:23,367 --> 00:59:25,533
I don't think
she loves me yet,

1314
00:59:25,567 --> 00:59:27,533
but perhaps with you gone,

1315
00:59:27,567 --> 00:59:30,500
she will see things in a more
realistic light in time.

1316
00:59:30,533 --> 00:59:33,167
Well, how can we get my suit
into the open?

1317
00:59:33,200 --> 00:59:35,100
I have some men I can trust.

1318
00:59:35,133 --> 00:59:36,600
- And sessom?
- No.

1319
00:59:36,633 --> 00:59:38,533
This movie is a filibuster!

1320
00:59:38,567 --> 00:59:40,467
He must never know,

1321
00:59:40,500 --> 00:59:43,000
otherwise we both
will be put to death.

1322
00:59:49,333 --> 00:59:51,400
Two nights a week,
I'm alone

1323
00:59:51,433 --> 00:59:54,167
and in complete charge
of the master control center.

1324
00:59:54,200 --> 00:59:55,667
- Can one man handle it?
- Yeah.

1325
00:59:55,700 --> 00:59:58,067
- Then why don't you do it?
- And on one of those nights

1326
00:59:58,100 --> 01:00:00,533
in the near future
while sessom is sleeping,

1327
01:00:00,567 --> 01:00:03,933
I will maneuver rheton
within a distance
of your earth's moon.

1328
01:00:03,967 --> 01:00:05,867
Do you think
they'll be able to see US?

1329
01:00:05,900 --> 01:00:07,367
Precisely.

1330
01:00:07,400 --> 01:00:09,200
They will investigate
and find you.

1331
01:00:09,233 --> 01:00:11,133
[High-pitched, sustained tone
alarm sounding]

1332
01:00:11,167 --> 01:00:14,133
Oh, no!
My pet cicada's in trouble!

1333
01:00:14,167 --> 01:00:17,067
Oh, man!
Kenny g's at it again!

1334
01:00:17,100 --> 01:00:19,067
[Alarm continues]

1335
01:00:19,100 --> 01:00:20,633
Go with her.

1336
01:00:20,667 --> 01:00:22,133
Go with who? What?
What do you--

1337
01:00:22,167 --> 01:00:23,500
oh, with her. Okay.

1338
01:00:23,533 --> 01:00:26,067
[Alarm continues]

1339
01:00:26,100 --> 01:00:29,067
- What is this?
- Our network is down.

1340
01:00:29,100 --> 01:00:30,733
What's happening?

1341
01:00:30,767 --> 01:00:32,900
The siren means
we're being attacked.

1342
01:00:32,933 --> 01:00:34,733
- Attacked by whom?
- I'm not saying.

1343
01:00:34,767 --> 01:00:37,067
You're mean to me.

1344
01:00:37,100 --> 01:00:39,067
Attacked by whom?

1345
01:00:39,100 --> 01:00:40,600
- The solarites.
- Duh!

1346
01:00:40,633 --> 01:00:42,967
We've been here too long.
They've discovered our position.

1347
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:45,967
- Who are the solarites?
- I've no time to explain.

1348
01:00:46,000 --> 01:00:48,267
- I must help sessom.
- Go back to bed, Chapman.

1349
01:00:48,300 --> 01:00:50,267
I'll wake you
if anything happens.

1350
01:00:50,300 --> 01:00:53,600
- What will this do
to our plans?
- Should I call the sitter?

1351
01:00:53,633 --> 01:00:56,167
We must fight this off,
or no one will have any plans.

1352
01:00:56,200 --> 01:00:58,333
Is everyone underground?

1353
01:00:58,367 --> 01:01:00,400
- Yes.
- Then we go.

1354
01:01:00,433 --> 01:01:02,467
[Imitating sessom]
And don't talk about
your secret plans

1355
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:04,600
in front of me.

1356
01:01:06,567 --> 01:01:08,667
Release the hush puppy.

1357
01:01:11,400 --> 01:01:13,067
[Gasps]
Hemorrhoids!

1358
01:01:13,100 --> 01:01:16,033
Get the tucks!

1359
01:01:16,067 --> 01:01:18,333
He's kool moe grandpa.

1360
01:01:21,067 --> 01:01:23,000
Oh, that helped.

1361
01:01:23,033 --> 01:01:25,533
- We're safe for the moment.
- Heil Hitler.

1362
01:01:25,567 --> 01:01:28,533
I fear they won't give up
so easily.

1363
01:01:28,567 --> 01:01:30,533
Safe for the moment?

1364
01:01:30,567 --> 01:01:33,200
Well, who are
these solarites anyhow?

1365
01:01:33,233 --> 01:01:35,200
- They are from a sun satellite.
- Oh.

1366
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:37,133
And for generations,
they've been after

1367
01:01:37,167 --> 01:01:39,700
our universal
gravity control,

1368
01:01:39,733 --> 01:01:42,133
'cause they want to avoid
being pulled into the sun.

1369
01:01:42,167 --> 01:01:44,267
If we don't stop them,

1370
01:01:44,300 --> 01:01:46,667
they'll eventually
attack your earth.

1371
01:01:46,700 --> 01:01:48,600
Then let's see you laugh.

1372
01:01:48,633 --> 01:01:50,700
Liara, show him the prisoner.

1373
01:01:50,733 --> 01:01:52,367
- [Chapman] Prisoner?
- Come.

1374
01:01:52,400 --> 01:01:54,367
We've got all the episodes
on tape.

1375
01:01:54,400 --> 01:01:56,667
It's a great show.

1376
01:01:56,700 --> 01:01:58,667
They're just taking him
off to daycare

1377
01:01:58,700 --> 01:02:01,367
while they straighten out
their little war.

1378
01:02:02,867 --> 01:02:05,400
The Beatles are playing
here tonight.

1379
01:02:08,033 --> 01:02:10,967
- [Imitating dog whining]
- Aw, puppy. Aw.

1380
01:02:11,000 --> 01:02:13,467
[Imitating dog panting]

1381
01:02:13,500 --> 01:02:15,467
So that's a solarite.

1382
01:02:15,500 --> 01:02:19,000
- Yes. He was captured
during the last war.
- [Imitating dog whining]

1383
01:02:19,033 --> 01:02:22,300
The only one of their monsters
that didn't die in the attack.

1384
01:02:22,333 --> 01:02:24,733
- When did this attack
take place?
- Several years ago,

1385
01:02:24,767 --> 01:02:26,867
when zetha was a little girl.

1386
01:02:26,900 --> 01:02:29,033
- That's when
she lost her voice.
- [Growls]

1387
01:02:29,067 --> 01:02:31,400
Whoo-hoo! Yeah!

1388
01:02:31,433 --> 01:02:33,400
What makes
those rocks disintegrate?

1389
01:02:33,433 --> 01:02:36,100
- [Crashing sound]
- [Scoffs] Weenie.

1390
01:02:36,133 --> 01:02:38,267
[Chapman]
It's as if they were hitting
some invisible wall.

1391
01:02:38,300 --> 01:02:40,767
That's exactly what it is.

1392
01:02:40,800 --> 01:02:42,967
- The monster is so strong
- [whoops]

1393
01:02:43,000 --> 01:02:44,967
That it would smash
any ordinary structure.

1394
01:02:45,000 --> 01:02:47,300
And what you call
an invisible wall

1395
01:02:47,333 --> 01:02:50,867
is really another way that we
use our gravitational control.

1396
01:02:50,900 --> 01:02:54,000
Now, by using
a high magnetic field,

1397
01:02:54,033 --> 01:02:56,667
we can lock molecules
so closely together

1398
01:02:56,700 --> 01:02:58,333
that they form a solid wall.

1399
01:02:58,367 --> 01:02:59,833
Whatever. It's fine.
[Whoops]

1400
01:02:59,867 --> 01:03:02,700
- A big hit at m.I.T.
- Where?

1401
01:03:02,733 --> 01:03:05,033
One of earth's more advanced
centers of learning.

1402
01:03:05,067 --> 01:03:07,100
A lot of pocketed,
short-sleeved shirts.

1403
01:03:07,133 --> 01:03:11,233
I only hope your wall
will hold him in check.

1404
01:03:11,267 --> 01:03:14,733
[Liara]
Yes. He could kill US all
if he escaped.

1405
01:03:14,767 --> 01:03:16,933
- [Imitating dog whining]
- Life on other planets...

1406
01:03:16,967 --> 01:03:18,433
[Scoffs]
What a crock!

1407
01:03:18,467 --> 01:03:20,267
And we were always wondering
if ours

1408
01:03:20,300 --> 01:03:22,567
was the only one so blessed.

1409
01:03:22,600 --> 01:03:25,067
There are many inhabited worlds,

1410
01:03:25,100 --> 01:03:27,900
but only these fire people
bother US.

1411
01:03:27,933 --> 01:03:31,100
We just need a place to scoot.

1412
01:03:31,133 --> 01:03:33,300
He's just a shar-pei
with a parted afro,

1413
01:03:33,333 --> 01:03:35,133
wearing a pizza slicer.

1414
01:03:36,900 --> 01:03:39,267
[Man on radio]
We have been sighted
by the enemy.

1415
01:03:39,300 --> 01:03:41,267
We are forming
a concentrated attack.

1416
01:03:41,300 --> 01:03:44,000
Pattern 6, vernier index 1-2.

1417
01:03:44,033 --> 01:03:45,333
Pattern 6?

1418
01:03:45,367 --> 01:03:47,833
We never attacked
on that one before.

1419
01:03:47,867 --> 01:03:50,800
They're hurling
flaming milk-bones at them.

1420
01:03:53,200 --> 01:03:54,833
What are we going to do?

1421
01:03:54,867 --> 01:03:56,800
We must try to break up
the attack.

1422
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:58,933
[Scoffs]
Thanks, patton.

1423
01:03:58,967 --> 01:04:02,267
I doubt the audience would enjoy
looking at a lump.

1424
01:04:02,300 --> 01:04:03,800
[Chuckling]

1425
01:04:03,833 --> 01:04:07,600
The worst they'll ever do
is hump their legs.

1426
01:04:07,633 --> 01:04:10,233
Oh, my engine light is on.
I wonder why.

1427
01:04:10,267 --> 01:04:12,533
[Solarite roaring]

1428
01:04:12,567 --> 01:04:15,200
They attack
in flaming pet taxis.

1429
01:04:15,233 --> 01:04:17,700
[Imitating sessom]
Oh, I just floated
an air biscuit.

1430
01:04:17,733 --> 01:04:19,600
I'm out of here.

1431
01:04:23,667 --> 01:04:26,633
- [Chants in Latin]
- [Equipment whirring]

1432
01:04:26,667 --> 01:04:28,933
[Imitating dogs barking]

1433
01:04:31,033 --> 01:04:33,333
Well, maybe if they didn't
disguise the planet

1434
01:04:33,367 --> 01:04:36,833
as a chicken mcnugget,
the dogs wouldn't attack it.

1435
01:04:36,867 --> 01:04:38,967
[Imitating goofy]
Don't be afraid.
We all have our shots.

1436
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:40,333
[Guffaws]

1437
01:04:40,367 --> 01:04:42,467
Where's a fire extinguisher
on this thing?

1438
01:04:45,033 --> 01:04:47,267
It's fantastic.

1439
01:04:47,300 --> 01:04:49,067
We can do one of two things.

1440
01:04:49,100 --> 01:04:51,267
- Scream or run.
- Outrun them or fight them.

1441
01:04:51,300 --> 01:04:53,733
Breaking up a formation
is one thing,

1442
01:04:53,767 --> 01:04:55,400
but how can you fight them?

1443
01:04:55,433 --> 01:04:57,733
- Do you have a chance?
- We have to settle that

1444
01:04:57,767 --> 01:04:59,233
once and for all.

1445
01:04:59,267 --> 01:05:02,067
Living in constant danger
isn't worthy of US.

1446
01:05:02,100 --> 01:05:05,733
Don't forget-- we still have
the gravity control.

1447
01:05:05,767 --> 01:05:09,800
The greatest danger to US
is the high-intensity heat bomb.

1448
01:05:09,833 --> 01:05:11,233
- He's right.
- Yeah.

1449
01:05:11,267 --> 01:05:12,800
They have enough
concentrated heat

1450
01:05:12,833 --> 01:05:14,800
to blow up
our planet instantly.

1451
01:05:14,833 --> 01:05:17,667
- What would you do?
- You make the call.

1452
01:05:17,700 --> 01:05:20,500
- I would fight.
- And you?

1453
01:05:20,533 --> 01:05:23,433
- Um, pass.
- Fight.

1454
01:05:23,467 --> 01:05:26,867
Right. That's exactly
my decision.

1455
01:05:37,467 --> 01:05:39,333
Okay. Not quite but almost.

1456
01:05:39,367 --> 01:05:41,200
- Let's try it again, shall we?
- Yeah. Okay.

1457
01:05:41,233 --> 01:05:42,533
- Okay, okay.
- [Clearing throat]

1458
01:05:42,567 --> 01:05:43,800
Okay, okay.

1459
01:05:43,833 --> 01:05:45,867
- **
- * twink

1460
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:47,967
um... oh, yeah.

1461
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:50,367
- * El
- **

1462
01:05:50,400 --> 01:05:52,700
- * twink
- **

1463
01:05:52,733 --> 01:05:55,133
uh, yeah, yeah. Uh...

1464
01:05:55,167 --> 01:05:57,967
- * El
- **

1465
01:05:58,000 --> 01:06:00,133
- * lit
- **

1466
01:06:00,167 --> 01:06:02,133
uh... mm...

1467
01:06:02,167 --> 01:06:04,233
- * El
- **

1468
01:06:04,267 --> 01:06:05,967
- * star
- ** [high-pitched tone]

1469
01:06:06,000 --> 01:06:07,700
- Whoa! [Mutters]
- [Laughs]

1470
01:06:07,733 --> 01:06:09,367
But, still,
we got seven notes in.

1471
01:06:09,400 --> 01:06:10,767
- That's a new record.
- That's pretty good.

1472
01:06:10,800 --> 01:06:12,567
- Hey, guys, what's up?
- Hey, Mike,

1473
01:06:12,600 --> 01:06:15,133
Tom and I saw those little
glass arrangement doohickys

1474
01:06:15,167 --> 01:06:16,933
they use to control gravity
in the movie.

1475
01:06:16,967 --> 01:06:19,600
- Yeah.
- And we remembered we shared
a true passion

1476
01:06:19,633 --> 01:06:21,333
for water glass rim music.

1477
01:06:21,367 --> 01:06:24,400
- Okay.
- And we've gotten pretty
darn great at it too.

1478
01:06:24,433 --> 01:06:27,433
Hey, Mike,
you wanna give it a try?
It sure is challenging.

1479
01:06:27,467 --> 01:06:29,200
No, no, no.
I'd just embarrass myself.

1480
01:06:29,233 --> 01:06:30,767
- Oh, go on.
- Come on.

1481
01:06:30,800 --> 01:06:32,933
I mean, we've practiced and all.
That's why we're good.

1482
01:06:32,967 --> 01:06:34,867
But we won't judge you
too harshly.

1483
01:06:34,900 --> 01:06:37,033
- Yeah.
- I-- oh, okay.

1484
01:06:37,067 --> 01:06:39,467
- If you put it that way,
I'll give it a shot.
- Okay.

1485
01:06:39,500 --> 01:06:41,633
** [classical piece]

1486
01:06:47,533 --> 01:06:48,933
Huh.

1487
01:06:50,433 --> 01:06:52,133
Huh.

1488
01:06:52,167 --> 01:06:54,567
** [continues]

1489
01:06:54,600 --> 01:06:56,467
- Huh.
- Huh.

1490
01:06:58,233 --> 01:06:59,667
Uh-huh.

1491
01:06:59,700 --> 01:07:01,333
[Inhales, exhales deeply]

1492
01:07:01,367 --> 01:07:03,700
- Yeah. Well...
- Uh, uh-huh...

1493
01:07:03,733 --> 01:07:06,667
Ah, you know, that's, uh--
that's about all I know.

1494
01:07:06,700 --> 01:07:08,467
- Yeah.
- You're right, though.
It's really fun.

1495
01:07:08,500 --> 01:07:10,733
And later on, would you guys
give me some more pointers?

1496
01:07:10,767 --> 01:07:12,733
- I'd appreciate it.
- Yeah, yeah.
A lot later, Mike.

1497
01:07:12,767 --> 01:07:15,333
Right now, we have to, uh,
feed the cat.

1498
01:07:15,367 --> 01:07:17,333
Well, get a cat and feed it.

1499
01:07:17,367 --> 01:07:18,833
Okay, well,
I'll see you later.

1500
01:07:18,867 --> 01:07:20,833
** [humming classical piece]

1501
01:07:20,867 --> 01:07:23,900
- [Scoffing]
- Huh.

1502
01:07:23,933 --> 01:07:27,533
Well, let him try tackling
"twinkle, twinkle,
little star" sometime, huh?

1503
01:07:27,567 --> 01:07:29,233
- Yeah, that's right!
- Try that, huh?

1504
01:07:29,267 --> 01:07:31,067
- One more time.
- Yes. Yes. Let's do it.

1505
01:07:31,100 --> 01:07:32,400
- Okay.
- Um...

1506
01:07:32,433 --> 01:07:34,333
- **
- * twink

1507
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:37,167
- * El
- ** [high-pitched tone]

1508
01:07:37,200 --> 01:07:39,133
- [Exclaims]
- Oh, darn! Geez!

1509
01:07:45,800 --> 01:07:47,867
- Prepare for battle.
- [Sighs]

1510
01:07:47,900 --> 01:07:50,567
- Sharp acceleration
for attack position.
- [Mike muttering]

1511
01:07:50,600 --> 01:07:52,233
[Groans]

1512
01:07:52,267 --> 01:07:56,367
Shake 'n bake,
and I death.

1513
01:07:56,400 --> 01:07:59,900
Wow, a tight turning radius
on that chicken thing there.

1514
01:08:02,433 --> 01:08:04,900
So they're just using
old six-shooters, huh?

1515
01:08:04,933 --> 01:08:06,900
Shootin' irons.

1516
01:08:06,933 --> 01:08:09,767
[Imitating gunshots]

1517
01:08:09,800 --> 01:08:12,400
It's no good.
Their defense is too crispy.

1518
01:08:12,433 --> 01:08:13,533
Dang.

1519
01:08:16,967 --> 01:08:19,200
Pathetic, huh?

1520
01:08:20,733 --> 01:08:24,433
Oh, don't tell me.
I'm out of rocks. Damn.

1521
01:08:24,467 --> 01:08:28,067
I'll gently pat these rocks
as a sign of protest.

1522
01:08:31,567 --> 01:08:34,533
On my bark. Woof!

1523
01:08:38,033 --> 01:08:41,167
We've got to Mark this planet.

1524
01:08:43,900 --> 01:08:45,667
[Imitating dog whining]

1525
01:08:45,700 --> 01:08:47,733
- Huh?
- [Equipment whirring]

1526
01:08:47,767 --> 01:08:51,333
Activate the gravity curtain.

1527
01:08:51,367 --> 01:08:54,133
Or the venetian gravity blinds.

1528
01:08:54,167 --> 01:08:55,633
Get off my foot.

1529
01:08:55,667 --> 01:08:58,733
** [humming]

1530
01:09:00,733 --> 01:09:03,633
Remember these people?
They're in our film.

1531
01:09:05,900 --> 01:09:08,033
I'm working my magic.

1532
01:09:13,167 --> 01:09:16,067
Oh, it was
a magnificent victory!

1533
01:09:16,100 --> 01:09:18,633
But I'm deeply plagued
with regret

1534
01:09:18,667 --> 01:09:20,767
- [laughter]
- ...When I'm forced to destroy.

1535
01:09:20,800 --> 01:09:23,233
- Yeah.
- If it wasn't them,
it would've been you.

1536
01:09:23,267 --> 01:09:25,000
Perhaps you are right.

1537
01:09:25,033 --> 01:09:27,000
- You are wise, Chapman.
- [Chuckles]

1538
01:09:27,033 --> 01:09:30,067
- One day, you and herron
will lead our people.
- Yes.

1539
01:09:30,100 --> 01:09:33,667
- I'm grateful, but--
- I will teach him
all he needs to know.

1540
01:09:33,700 --> 01:09:34,867
Oh.

1541
01:09:34,900 --> 01:09:36,533
[Imitating goofy]
Oh, hey, it worked.

1542
01:09:36,567 --> 01:09:38,333
Mama solarite
didn't raise no dummies.

1543
01:09:38,367 --> 01:09:39,800
[Guffaws]

1544
01:09:41,933 --> 01:09:44,833
Go on. Go on.

1545
01:09:46,533 --> 01:09:48,000
He's an elderly solarite.

1546
01:09:48,033 --> 01:09:49,967
- He has trouble with stairs.
- Yeah.

1547
01:09:50,000 --> 01:09:51,667
Where's zetha?

1548
01:09:51,700 --> 01:09:53,533
- She went to sleep early.
- [Laughter]

1549
01:09:53,567 --> 01:09:56,367
Sleep. I'm very tired.

1550
01:09:56,400 --> 01:10:00,133
Perhaps the battle was too much
of a strain on me.
Good night.

1551
01:10:00,167 --> 01:10:01,900
- Good night, father.
- Sleep well, sessom.

1552
01:10:01,933 --> 01:10:04,967
There's a sustacal
with my name on it.

1553
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:07,700
[Imitating sessom]
I'm gonna go drive around
and leave the blinker on.

1554
01:10:07,733 --> 01:10:09,300
[Chuckles]

1555
01:10:09,333 --> 01:10:11,600
I'll just hide out here

1556
01:10:11,633 --> 01:10:14,033
at Fred and Wilma's house.

1557
01:10:17,533 --> 01:10:19,700
[Scoffs]
Ma'am, could you quit writhing

1558
01:10:19,733 --> 01:10:21,767
on the coffee table?

1559
01:10:23,433 --> 01:10:26,267
Huh. Their bed technology
is light years behind

1560
01:10:26,300 --> 01:10:29,033
their space-going chicken
technology.

1561
01:10:31,733 --> 01:10:33,800
Uh, excuse me, ma'am.
I don't mean to bother you.

1562
01:10:33,833 --> 01:10:37,800
Do you have any Liv-a snaps
or perhaps a beggin' strip?

1563
01:10:37,833 --> 01:10:40,033
Think he's been backpacking
through Europe?

1564
01:10:40,067 --> 01:10:41,667
[Mutters]

1565
01:10:43,033 --> 01:10:45,067
Uh, ma'am, I realize
you don't know me,

1566
01:10:45,100 --> 01:10:48,033
but I really need
to go walkies.

1567
01:10:50,567 --> 01:10:52,467
Oh, honey,
you look flush.

1568
01:10:52,500 --> 01:10:54,833
Let me feel your nose.

1569
01:10:54,867 --> 01:10:56,533
Oh. Hmm.

1570
01:10:56,567 --> 01:10:58,667
Oh, I bet you shed.
I shed.

1571
01:10:58,700 --> 01:11:01,067
Do you shed?

1572
01:11:02,167 --> 01:11:04,067
Last call, everybody.
Last call.

1573
01:11:04,100 --> 01:11:05,567
Come on.

1574
01:11:05,600 --> 01:11:08,100
Okay, okay. Her hair
controls the light switch.

1575
01:11:08,133 --> 01:11:10,867
I touch her hair,
the lights go out. Got it.

1576
01:11:12,467 --> 01:11:15,467
I know. I'll try
submissive urination.

1577
01:11:17,967 --> 01:11:21,733
He's basically a cauliflower
with a handle and eyes.

1578
01:11:25,933 --> 01:11:28,900
Ew, it smells
like wet fur in here.

1579
01:11:28,933 --> 01:11:33,000
She forgets she's mute
and thinks she's blind.

1580
01:11:33,033 --> 01:11:34,833
** [humming along
with soundtrack]

1581
01:11:36,133 --> 01:11:38,533
You have a kind face.

1582
01:11:38,567 --> 01:11:40,533
** [Mike humming]

1583
01:11:40,567 --> 01:11:42,467
** [Tom servo
imitating drumbeats]

1584
01:11:42,500 --> 01:11:45,433
Yo. Word.

1585
01:11:45,467 --> 01:11:48,733
Here's the ginger
you ordered, ma'am.

1586
01:11:50,267 --> 01:11:53,800
Uh, I can't get away
from the lumbering slow thing.

1587
01:11:53,833 --> 01:11:57,167
Whoa, she's screaming
her fingers off right now.

1588
01:11:57,200 --> 01:12:00,100
I'm gonna terrify her
with the hand thing.

1589
01:12:02,500 --> 01:12:04,967
I had suction cups
put on my fingers.

1590
01:12:05,000 --> 01:12:06,633
Seemed like a good idea
at the time.

1591
01:12:08,900 --> 01:12:12,233
So, apparently women are devoid
of the fight-or-flight reflex.

1592
01:12:12,267 --> 01:12:14,033
Yeah, they only have
the fainting reflex.

1593
01:12:14,067 --> 01:12:16,533
- [Scoffs]
- Women! [Scoffs]

1594
01:12:18,200 --> 01:12:19,667
No more frisbee catching.

1595
01:12:19,700 --> 01:12:22,400
I'm on a whole
nother level now.

1596
01:12:25,333 --> 01:12:28,500
The monster dresses
like Carol Channing.

1597
01:12:29,567 --> 01:12:31,800
Uh, wait, wait.
Did I leave any clothes?

1598
01:12:31,833 --> 01:12:34,500
Doh! I piddled in the corner.

1599
01:12:36,367 --> 01:12:39,600
Commander spot
will be very pleased.

1600
01:12:42,000 --> 01:12:44,733
Where the hell is the elevator?

1601
01:12:44,767 --> 01:12:48,333
So I got her now,
and I haven't the slightest idea
what to do with her.

1602
01:12:48,367 --> 01:12:50,067
[Guffaws]

1603
01:12:51,867 --> 01:12:54,867
Tsk. Hang on.
I'm gonna get a two-Wheeler.

1604
01:12:58,467 --> 01:13:02,067
Nurse! Nurse!

1605
01:13:02,100 --> 01:13:04,700
Okay, okay, okay.
Everything's cool.

1606
01:13:04,733 --> 01:13:06,833
I'm not gonna beat myself up
over this.

1607
01:13:09,867 --> 01:13:11,600
- [Imitating dino from
the flintstones barking]
- Dino, no!

1608
01:13:11,633 --> 01:13:14,633
- What was that?
- It's over there.

1609
01:13:14,667 --> 01:13:16,800
Yeah, I guess their raucous
postwar celebration

1610
01:13:16,833 --> 01:13:18,533
will have to wait.

1611
01:13:19,867 --> 01:13:22,000
You wash my face off
with snow.

1612
01:13:22,033 --> 01:13:24,467
There. Found my Mark. Good.

1613
01:13:24,500 --> 01:13:26,367
- [Sessom] Help.
- Sessom!

1614
01:13:26,400 --> 01:13:28,367
- Oh, father!
- He licked me all over!

1615
01:13:28,400 --> 01:13:29,867
Oh, father!

1616
01:13:29,900 --> 01:13:32,333
- What happened to him?
- I think it was the solarite.

1617
01:13:32,367 --> 01:13:34,433
- Are you all right?
- I...

1618
01:13:34,467 --> 01:13:37,400
- What happened?
- I don't know.

1619
01:13:37,433 --> 01:13:40,400
Was it the solarite?
Did you see him?

1620
01:13:40,433 --> 01:13:42,933
- It was terrible.
- [Chuckles]

1621
01:13:42,967 --> 01:13:46,800
I pushed down an old guy
for you, darling.

1622
01:13:46,833 --> 01:13:49,400
We'll build a split-level
with a doggie door.

1623
01:13:49,433 --> 01:13:53,333
I'll fetch the paper for you
every day.

1624
01:13:53,367 --> 01:13:55,400
Okay, I'm gonna go bark
for no reason,

1625
01:13:55,433 --> 01:13:57,267
lick myself
and eat grass till I vomit,

1626
01:13:57,300 --> 01:14:01,233
then I'll be back.
[Guffaws]

1627
01:14:01,267 --> 01:14:02,567
[Whirring]

1628
01:14:02,600 --> 01:14:04,333
Okay, what'd I do?

1629
01:14:06,367 --> 01:14:07,500
[Whirring]

1630
01:14:07,533 --> 01:14:10,867
Whoa. I'm way out
of my league now.

1631
01:14:10,900 --> 01:14:12,733
[Herron]
I'm going to the control room.

1632
01:14:12,767 --> 01:14:15,167
[Chapman]
No, you stay with liara.

1633
01:14:15,200 --> 01:14:17,233
- Chapman!
- Yes?

1634
01:14:17,267 --> 01:14:19,933
How far do you think you'd be
if I hadn't called you back?

1635
01:14:19,967 --> 01:14:21,867
Go through that corridor.
It's shorter.

1636
01:14:21,900 --> 01:14:23,067
- Right.
- But be careful.

1637
01:14:23,100 --> 01:14:24,633
And button your blouse.

1638
01:14:24,667 --> 01:14:26,933
- I'll be all right.
- Oh, herron.

1639
01:14:26,967 --> 01:14:28,400
[Sniffing]

1640
01:14:28,433 --> 01:14:30,867
Ooh, they have dogs. Ew.

1641
01:14:32,400 --> 01:14:34,700
Zetha, are you all right?

1642
01:14:34,733 --> 01:14:36,167
Um, excuse me. I--
[Clears throat]

1643
01:14:36,200 --> 01:14:39,467
I have the element of,
uh, surprise over you.

1644
01:14:39,500 --> 01:14:40,800
[Zetha screams]

1645
01:14:40,833 --> 01:14:43,800
It's a good guard dog,
you have to admit.

1646
01:14:43,833 --> 01:14:45,300
Okay, hang on.

1647
01:14:45,333 --> 01:14:46,867
On my way.
Be right there.

1648
01:14:46,900 --> 01:14:48,600
Hang on.
Just a minute.

1649
01:14:48,633 --> 01:14:50,167
Nice puppy.
[Nervous chuckle]
Good dog.

1650
01:14:50,200 --> 01:14:52,167
Just let me turn around
and present my butt to you.

1651
01:14:52,200 --> 01:14:55,467
I think you'll find
everything in order.
[Nervous chuckle]

1652
01:14:55,500 --> 01:14:57,967
- Hey! Watch the plates!
- [Screams]

1653
01:14:58,000 --> 01:15:00,833
Anybody could just dematerialize
themselves by accident.

1654
01:15:00,867 --> 01:15:02,667
Maybe they should
cordon it off or something.

1655
01:15:02,700 --> 01:15:04,667
Yeah.

1656
01:15:04,700 --> 01:15:09,133
They should scratch his belly
till his leg shakes
to subdue him.

1657
01:15:09,167 --> 01:15:10,733
You're it!

1658
01:15:10,767 --> 01:15:12,633
Come on!
I tagged you!

1659
01:15:12,667 --> 01:15:15,067
[Solarite growling]

1660
01:15:15,100 --> 01:15:16,567
Sorry.

1661
01:15:18,067 --> 01:15:20,067
Hang on. I'm not quite--
okay, there we go.

1662
01:15:20,100 --> 01:15:22,000
[Screeching]

1663
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:26,967
Good night, everybody.
Minneapolis rocks.

1664
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:29,300
Big hand for the solarite band.
Come on.

1665
01:15:29,333 --> 01:15:32,833
* Shannon is gone, I see

1666
01:15:32,867 --> 01:15:36,533
huh. Next time
we're getting a cat.

1667
01:15:36,567 --> 01:15:40,200
Not a "dangerous" sign?
Rope it off? Anything?

1668
01:15:40,233 --> 01:15:42,400
Nope.

1669
01:15:42,433 --> 01:15:45,100
All dogs go to hell.

1670
01:15:47,167 --> 01:15:49,000
We're friends now. Why?

1671
01:15:49,033 --> 01:15:50,367
How's sessom?

1672
01:15:50,400 --> 01:15:52,233
He will be all right.
Liara's with him.

1673
01:15:52,267 --> 01:15:53,267
I'm glad.

1674
01:15:53,300 --> 01:15:55,200
You still wish to return
to your world?

1675
01:15:55,233 --> 01:15:57,233
- Yes, but--
- well, then, tonight's
the best time.

1676
01:15:57,267 --> 01:16:00,467
The chaos of battle
has brought US closer to
your moon than we've ever been.

1677
01:16:00,500 --> 01:16:03,033
- Really?
- It'll be a simple task
to maneuver rheton slowly

1678
01:16:03,067 --> 01:16:05,267
- ...and steadily even closer,
and the risk will not be great--
- it will?

1679
01:16:05,300 --> 01:16:07,433
- ...because the travel time
will be short.
- This is fascinating!

1680
01:16:07,467 --> 01:16:09,433
It will be well within
the range of the moon's radar?

1681
01:16:09,467 --> 01:16:11,667
- Yes, but we cannot
go unnoticed.
- Come on.

1682
01:16:11,700 --> 01:16:14,433
- Now, as soon as we're within
range of your moon--
- okay.

1683
01:16:14,467 --> 01:16:17,267
- ...my men will carry
your suit out into the open.
- I gotta go fold some socks.

1684
01:16:17,300 --> 01:16:18,867
- If your people come
to investigate--
- this is riveting!

1685
01:16:18,900 --> 01:16:20,933
...we'll pull them
into our gravity
and direct their landing.

1686
01:16:20,967 --> 01:16:23,400
- Meanwhile,
you will enter your suit--
- wow. No!

1687
01:16:23,433 --> 01:16:26,733
...seal it up
so that you're not exposed
to our atmosphere, and...

1688
01:16:26,767 --> 01:16:28,667
- Well, the rest you know.
- This is fascinating!

1689
01:16:28,700 --> 01:16:30,467
- Where shall I meet you?
- In the control chamber.

1690
01:16:30,500 --> 01:16:33,067
- Someone will come for you.
- Wow.

1691
01:16:39,333 --> 01:16:41,967
I hogged out on a baby carrot.

1692
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:44,200
I need to walk it off.

1693
01:16:44,233 --> 01:16:45,900
- Hi.
- Uh, get any better?

1694
01:16:45,933 --> 01:16:47,900
- Zetha.
- No.

1695
01:16:47,933 --> 01:16:49,233
It's you.

1696
01:16:49,267 --> 01:16:50,900
Yes, frank Chapman.

1697
01:16:50,933 --> 01:16:52,900
- But you can talk.
- Son of a...

1698
01:16:52,933 --> 01:16:55,567
- Great.
- From my fright, when I thought
you were going to be killed,

1699
01:16:55,600 --> 01:16:57,500
something happened.

1700
01:16:57,533 --> 01:17:01,667
And after I screamed,
I found I was able to speak.

1701
01:17:01,700 --> 01:17:03,867
- Zetha...
- Hey, I'm talking here!

1702
01:17:03,900 --> 01:17:06,700
- I have many things to say
to you, frank Chapman.
- Like "pickle."

1703
01:17:06,733 --> 01:17:09,367
It's so wonderful--
you being able to talk.

1704
01:17:09,400 --> 01:17:11,367
And I have so many things
to say to you.

1705
01:17:11,400 --> 01:17:12,833
Like "I think
we should break up."

1706
01:17:12,867 --> 01:17:14,567
Oh, everything
has been terrible.

1707
01:17:14,600 --> 01:17:17,600
Especially that lunch.
Ew. It was awful.

1708
01:17:17,633 --> 01:17:19,600
You're so lovely.

1709
01:17:19,633 --> 01:17:21,867
You have such
an adorable little face.

1710
01:17:21,900 --> 01:17:24,267
I think I'll jam
my tongue into it.

1711
01:17:26,067 --> 01:17:28,400
Boy, she is earning combat pay.

1712
01:17:28,433 --> 01:17:30,400
- Yep.
- Whoo.

1713
01:17:30,433 --> 01:17:35,167
And she's horrified
back into muteness.

1714
01:17:35,200 --> 01:17:38,200
- Isn't it strange?
- You haven't called
the police yet.

1715
01:17:38,233 --> 01:17:41,167
Here in this place,
I have found perhaps

1716
01:17:41,200 --> 01:17:43,000
what I've been looking for
all my life.

1717
01:17:43,033 --> 01:17:46,433
- Pancakes.
- And I must leave.

1718
01:17:46,467 --> 01:17:49,267
Although everything within me
wants to stay.

1719
01:17:49,300 --> 01:17:51,700
Especially my spleen.

1720
01:17:51,733 --> 01:17:54,033
It's my solemn duty to leave.

1721
01:17:54,067 --> 01:17:55,700
You understand that, don't you?

1722
01:17:55,733 --> 01:17:59,267
I'm sorry. Now I'm deaf.

1723
01:17:59,300 --> 01:18:01,333
Frank Chapman,
I've been in love with you

1724
01:18:01,367 --> 01:18:03,833
- ...since the first time
I saw you--
- ew.

1725
01:18:03,867 --> 01:18:06,433
...and I've never been able
to speak a word of it
until now.

1726
01:18:06,467 --> 01:18:08,767
Is he a turnip
that grew a face?

1727
01:18:08,800 --> 01:18:11,900
But as I know,
my love for you is so strong.

1728
01:18:11,933 --> 01:18:13,900
I can overcome my revulsion.

1729
01:18:13,933 --> 01:18:17,867
So I also know
that you will leave.

1730
01:18:17,900 --> 01:18:19,867
I must leave.

1731
01:18:19,900 --> 01:18:23,167
Hang on.
I wanna get my gum back.

1732
01:18:23,200 --> 01:18:25,200
Mm. Well, I see
you've been flossing.

1733
01:18:25,233 --> 01:18:27,033
That's good.

1734
01:18:29,767 --> 01:18:33,133
The word "love"
means detest, right?

1735
01:18:33,167 --> 01:18:35,133
Wow, the first thing
I ever say in my life,

1736
01:18:35,167 --> 01:18:38,133
and I blow it big-time.

1737
01:18:38,167 --> 01:18:39,800
Look, it's over.
Leave me alone.

1738
01:18:39,833 --> 01:18:41,333
It's over!

1739
01:18:41,367 --> 01:18:43,267
[Equipment whirring]

1740
01:18:45,333 --> 01:18:47,800
- Good. You're on time.
- For once.

1741
01:18:47,833 --> 01:18:50,400
- [Herron] Here we go.
- Let me hear you say "yeah."

1742
01:18:50,433 --> 01:18:52,400
- [Whirring intensifies]
- Another hour,

1743
01:18:52,433 --> 01:18:54,433
and we shall be close enough
for you to be found.

1744
01:18:54,467 --> 01:18:57,600
I'm just gonna drop you off
at the bus station.
I hope that's okay.

1745
01:18:57,633 --> 01:18:59,100
[Whirring continues]

1746
01:18:59,133 --> 01:19:02,133
Don't. Don't.
You're smothering me.

1747
01:19:04,933 --> 01:19:07,733
Delivery for Robert downey, Jr.

1748
01:19:09,733 --> 01:19:14,133
[Woman on radio]
Lunar base 1
to rocket ship 380. Over.

1749
01:19:14,167 --> 01:19:17,867
This is rocket ship 380
to lunar base 1. Over.

1750
01:19:17,900 --> 01:19:21,567
Radar has just picked up
a giant asteroid.
Identity unknown.

1751
01:19:21,600 --> 01:19:24,300
Cannot find any record of it
in the space charts.

1752
01:19:24,333 --> 01:19:26,167
The phantom planet.

1753
01:19:26,200 --> 01:19:28,633
Give US exact position
of asteroid.

1754
01:19:28,667 --> 01:19:31,000
Nine degrees
in northern cluster field.

1755
01:19:31,033 --> 01:19:33,200
And I have an order
from colonel lansfield.

1756
01:19:33,233 --> 01:19:35,233
You are to land
on this asteroid

1757
01:19:35,267 --> 01:19:37,167
and send white to investigate.

1758
01:19:37,200 --> 01:19:39,233
Immediately, young man.

1759
01:19:39,267 --> 01:19:41,167
I--

1760
01:19:41,200 --> 01:19:44,667
I hope you will find happiness
back with your people.

1761
01:19:44,700 --> 01:19:48,133
You would be my happiness...
If you were there.

1762
01:19:48,167 --> 01:19:50,700
You wanna live in my habitrail?

1763
01:19:50,733 --> 01:19:52,800
Frank Chapman, please...

1764
01:19:52,833 --> 01:19:54,800
You must take this stone.

1765
01:19:54,833 --> 01:19:56,400
And rub it in your armpits.

1766
01:19:56,433 --> 01:19:58,767
It will be a good luck charm.

1767
01:19:58,800 --> 01:20:00,133
Hold on to it.

1768
01:20:00,167 --> 01:20:03,867
It will help you to go back
safely to your people.

1769
01:20:03,900 --> 01:20:05,233
Keep it.

1770
01:20:05,267 --> 01:20:07,333
Oh, she's gonna
"just friend" him.

1771
01:20:07,367 --> 01:20:11,500
And remember my-- my love.

1772
01:20:11,533 --> 01:20:14,433
Yes, zetha.
I'll keep it forever.

1773
01:20:14,467 --> 01:20:16,200
In my junk drawer
in the basement.

1774
01:20:18,900 --> 01:20:20,533
I just confirmed it.

1775
01:20:20,567 --> 01:20:23,467
A rocket, similar to yours,
is heading in our direction.

1776
01:20:23,500 --> 01:20:25,600
- I hope they won't crash.
- Don't worry.

1777
01:20:25,633 --> 01:20:29,467
- It will.
- I have the best men
on gravitation control.

1778
01:20:29,500 --> 01:20:31,467
And I have another man
who's coming to help me

1779
01:20:31,500 --> 01:20:33,933
turn on the oxygen tanks
as soon as you're in your suit.

1780
01:20:33,967 --> 01:20:36,867
- [Tom servo mutters]
- Thank you, herron.

1781
01:20:36,900 --> 01:20:40,333
You know,
we've become friends here.

1782
01:20:40,367 --> 01:20:43,700
- Good friends.
- Which is why I bring up
my missing wallet.

1783
01:20:43,733 --> 01:20:46,267
We were
to become friends anywhere--

1784
01:20:46,300 --> 01:20:48,767
your planet or my earth.

1785
01:20:48,800 --> 01:20:50,100
[Groans]

1786
01:20:50,133 --> 01:20:51,767
I wish you and liara
much happiness.

1787
01:20:51,800 --> 01:20:54,700
This is longer than
a Minnesota good-bye.

1788
01:20:56,133 --> 01:20:58,200
Um, don't call,
'cause I don't have a phone,

1789
01:20:58,233 --> 01:21:00,200
and don't write
'cause we don't have mail here.

1790
01:21:00,233 --> 01:21:01,533
And I don't have e-mail.

1791
01:21:01,567 --> 01:21:04,967
Look, I'm just really hard
to get ahold of.

1792
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:07,633
Whew! I thought I was gonna see
that giant pink tongue

1793
01:21:07,667 --> 01:21:09,700
coming at me again.

1794
01:21:11,600 --> 01:21:14,300
Uh, a lot of animals
got in here,
used it for their toilet.

1795
01:21:14,333 --> 01:21:17,133
We tried to clean
most of it out.

1796
01:21:17,167 --> 01:21:19,000
Okay, in you go. Whoa.

1797
01:21:19,033 --> 01:21:21,200
Check this out.
He's nude!

1798
01:21:21,233 --> 01:21:22,667
Oh, man.

1799
01:21:24,133 --> 01:21:26,800
Just one more peek. Wow.

1800
01:21:26,833 --> 01:21:29,900
Whew. He almost stayed.

1801
01:21:29,933 --> 01:21:31,900
Oh-- oh, wait, wait, wait.

1802
01:21:31,933 --> 01:21:33,900
My thumb is bent back in here.
Ow! Ooh!

1803
01:21:33,933 --> 01:21:36,633
My leg is all twisted.
Ow! Ooh!

1804
01:21:38,000 --> 01:21:40,567
Yeah, the movie's circling
the drain at this point.

1805
01:21:40,600 --> 01:21:43,767
- Yep.
- I find you guilty as charged.

1806
01:21:43,800 --> 01:21:46,233
- [Women shouting] Kill him!
- [Tom servo mutters]

1807
01:21:46,267 --> 01:21:48,067
You'll never see
your world again.

1808
01:21:48,100 --> 01:21:50,400
Come on! We didn't like
these scenes the first time!

1809
01:21:50,433 --> 01:21:52,533
Yeah.

1810
01:21:52,567 --> 01:21:55,600
What if his flashbacks
lap themselves?

1811
01:21:57,400 --> 01:21:59,600
[Imitating goofy]
Can I go out, please?

1812
01:22:01,567 --> 01:22:05,000
Frank Chapman,
I've been in love with you
since the first time I saw you.

1813
01:22:05,033 --> 01:22:08,400
No fair! You can't flashback
to stuff we saw 10 seconds ago!

1814
01:22:08,433 --> 01:22:09,933
Yeah.

1815
01:22:09,967 --> 01:22:11,733
Chapman. Chapman!

1816
01:22:11,767 --> 01:22:14,467
- You got any gum?
- White to beecher.

1817
01:22:14,500 --> 01:22:16,233
Come in, white.

1818
01:22:16,267 --> 01:22:18,133
I found Chapman.
He's alive.

1819
01:22:19,367 --> 01:22:22,367
But there's no trace
of makonnen.

1820
01:22:22,400 --> 01:22:24,367
Where's makonnen?

1821
01:22:24,400 --> 01:22:26,867
He's dead. He's gone.

1822
01:22:26,900 --> 01:22:31,167
He kept yapping about beauty,
so I shot him out the air lock.

1823
01:22:31,200 --> 01:22:34,233
Oh, I am so jammed up
in my cup right now.

1824
01:22:34,267 --> 01:22:35,767
Oh!

1825
01:22:36,800 --> 01:22:39,500
Where are we?

1826
01:22:39,533 --> 01:22:41,333
Where are they?

1827
01:22:41,367 --> 01:22:43,167
Where are the others?

1828
01:22:43,200 --> 01:22:45,100
And where's Waldo?
What about that whole issue?

1829
01:22:45,133 --> 01:22:46,433
Where's who?

1830
01:22:46,467 --> 01:22:47,633
Zetha.

1831
01:22:47,667 --> 01:22:49,567
What are you talking about?

1832
01:22:49,600 --> 01:22:52,733
Sessom, herron...

1833
01:22:52,767 --> 01:22:54,933
Man, you are nuttier
than an outhouse rat.

1834
01:22:54,967 --> 01:22:56,600
Come on.
Let's get back to the ship.

1835
01:22:56,633 --> 01:22:58,267
Hey, you wanna hear
something funny?

1836
01:22:58,300 --> 01:23:00,900
I found
a little dark-haired woman
on the bottom of my shoe.

1837
01:23:00,933 --> 01:23:02,233
[Chuckles]

1838
01:23:04,767 --> 01:23:06,400
White to beecher.

1839
01:23:06,433 --> 01:23:08,333
I'm bringing him in.

1840
01:23:08,367 --> 01:23:10,067
He seems to be all right.

1841
01:23:10,100 --> 01:23:11,867
He says makonnen is dead.

1842
01:23:11,900 --> 01:23:13,700
He keeps talking
about other people.

1843
01:23:13,733 --> 01:23:15,633
I think he's in
a state of shock.

1844
01:23:15,667 --> 01:23:16,967
Do you need assistance?

1845
01:23:17,000 --> 01:23:18,467
No, captain.
I can handle him alone.

1846
01:23:18,500 --> 01:23:20,467
Well, okay.

1847
01:23:20,500 --> 01:23:22,133
You know, frank,
you're a lucky guy.

1848
01:23:22,167 --> 01:23:24,133
You're going to
a nice federal prison.

1849
01:23:24,167 --> 01:23:26,733
This is a wandering planet.
Could've carried you anywhere.

1850
01:23:26,767 --> 01:23:29,133
East Lansing, crab nebula,
oxnard.

1851
01:23:29,167 --> 01:23:30,633
I'm sure glad we found you.

1852
01:23:30,667 --> 01:23:32,133
'Cause we ran out
of ugly guys.

1853
01:23:32,167 --> 01:23:33,767
Zetha...

1854
01:23:35,267 --> 01:23:37,400
Where is she?

1855
01:23:37,433 --> 01:23:39,400
What you need is rest.

1856
01:23:39,433 --> 01:23:42,133
And a stern lecture
about letting your partner die.

1857
01:23:43,267 --> 01:23:45,000
So, were you small
when you were gone?

1858
01:23:45,033 --> 01:23:47,633
'Cause you're acting
like you were really small.

1859
01:23:49,433 --> 01:23:51,667
I just wanna remind you
this is a northwest flight,

1860
01:23:51,700 --> 01:23:53,667
so we'll be sitting
on the tarmac for an hour

1861
01:23:53,700 --> 01:23:55,967
with no beverages
and air conditioning,
and we're out of meals,

1862
01:23:56,000 --> 01:23:58,067
and the flight attendants
are overworked and abusive,

1863
01:23:58,100 --> 01:24:00,567
and if you complain,
we'll throw you off the flight.

1864
01:24:00,600 --> 01:24:02,700
[Equipment beeping]

1865
01:24:04,267 --> 01:24:06,233
Prepare for immediate takeoff.

1866
01:24:06,267 --> 01:24:07,767
I am preparing
for immediate takeoff.

1867
01:24:07,800 --> 01:24:11,300
You see me preparing?
Taking off air tanks
is preparing.

1868
01:24:11,333 --> 01:24:13,233
How do you feel, Chapman?

1869
01:24:13,267 --> 01:24:14,767
I don't know.

1870
01:24:14,800 --> 01:24:16,833
I think I'm carsick.

1871
01:24:16,867 --> 01:24:18,500
I don't understand.

1872
01:24:18,533 --> 01:24:20,767
Why can't I have my sippy cup?

1873
01:24:20,800 --> 01:24:22,900
It's unbelievable.

1874
01:24:22,933 --> 01:24:25,900
[Beecher]
We'll get you back to moon base
for a thorough examination.

1875
01:24:25,933 --> 01:24:29,300
- And spanking.
- [Beecher]
Do you think you're hurt?

1876
01:24:29,333 --> 01:24:31,467
I don't think so.

1877
01:24:31,500 --> 01:24:33,800
[Beecher]
You must have been knocked out
for quite a while.

1878
01:24:33,833 --> 01:24:36,367
We hit you as hard
as we could.

1879
01:24:36,400 --> 01:24:38,800
I must have been dreaming.

1880
01:24:38,833 --> 01:24:41,333
Quite possible
you were delirious.

1881
01:24:41,367 --> 01:24:43,967
The shock of the crash-landing
of your ship.

1882
01:24:44,000 --> 01:24:45,300
Ray's gone.

1883
01:24:45,333 --> 01:24:47,833
Why don't we play the quiet game
when we take off, okay?

1884
01:24:47,867 --> 01:24:49,933
But I just left
zetha and herron.

1885
01:24:49,967 --> 01:24:52,100
They gave me rocks and stuff.

1886
01:24:53,567 --> 01:24:57,000
Well, I got a Grisham novel.
I gotta get started on that.

1887
01:24:59,567 --> 01:25:02,300
I should have gotten her
a stick.

1888
01:25:03,533 --> 01:25:05,433
She had such
an adorable little face.

1889
01:25:05,467 --> 01:25:08,567
Yeah, well,
so does Paul Williams,
but you don't French-kiss him!

1890
01:25:08,600 --> 01:25:11,133
All rockets ready for firing.
Stand by for countdown.

1891
01:25:11,167 --> 01:25:12,567
You guys wanna see my rock?

1892
01:25:12,600 --> 01:25:15,033
The gravity of this planetoid
is very strong.

1893
01:25:15,067 --> 01:25:17,333
We'll need every bit of thrust
for our takeoff.

1894
01:25:17,367 --> 01:25:19,133
- Don't worry.
- I've got extra thrust.

1895
01:25:19,167 --> 01:25:20,467
I know we're gonna make it.

1896
01:25:20,500 --> 01:25:21,867
[Beecher]
Start your countdown.

1897
01:25:21,900 --> 01:25:23,833
- [White] Ten, nine--
- right.

1898
01:25:23,867 --> 01:25:25,300
- ...eight--
- yeah.

1899
01:25:25,333 --> 01:25:27,233
- ...seven, six--
- let's get on with it.

1900
01:25:27,267 --> 01:25:29,200
- Mm-hmm.
- ...Five, four--

1901
01:25:29,233 --> 01:25:31,967
- pi!
- ...Three, two,

1902
01:25:32,000 --> 01:25:33,367
one, zero.

1903
01:25:33,400 --> 01:25:34,533
[Rocket engine blasts]

1904
01:25:34,567 --> 01:25:36,533
And they die.

1905
01:25:36,567 --> 01:25:39,300
Houston, we have a moron.
Over.

1906
01:25:42,133 --> 01:25:43,600
Cut off power.

1907
01:25:43,633 --> 01:25:45,300
Is that a good idea, Roy?

1908
01:25:45,333 --> 01:25:46,767
Power off.

1909
01:25:48,333 --> 01:25:50,300
The rear screen.

1910
